{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery","id":1336895,"title":"Homebrew Charms, Spells & Evocation Gallery","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-19T10:28:09-07:00","id":1336895,"title":"Homebrew Charms, Spells & Evocation Gallery","content":"Sometimes you're not trying to homebrew an entire system or charmset, you simply have a cool idea for a Charm - This is a place to share such Charms with others.<br /> <br /> To keep the thread focused, here are a few rules to follow :<br /> <br /> 1) Custom Charms should be self-contained or only have 1 or 2 related Charms. Full Charmsets and/or full reworks should go to a different thread (feel free to advertise those threads here)<br /> <br /> 2) Custom Evocations should be for published Artifacts, and like Charms they should be standalone, not full sets or full reworks. This thread isn't for homebrew Artifacts.<br /> <br /> 3) Spells are wecome, but Sorcerous workings should be directed to their dedicated thread <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/733522-sorcerous-workings-where-we-make-judgments\">here</a><br /> <br /> 4) Critiquing Charms is welcome, just be careful not to derail the thread with debates on specific Charms.<br /> <br /> Have fun!<br /> <br /> <br /> ------------<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Talent-Oozing Allure</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>-; <b>Mins:</b> Craft 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Bridge<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None or Any 3 Presence, Performance or Larceny Charms<br /> <br /> The Solar is so in tune with their crafting talents that others cannot help but recognize her calling. Others automatically see her as a craftswoman - that is, she can play on a Minor Intimacy to convince others that she is the right person to see if you need something crafted. Some people may even instinctively go towards her when they find themselves in need of an Artisan, even without knowing her, out of a sheer gut feeling. Note that this Charm's effect takes into account the Solar's Craft Abilities - No one will be naturally convinced that a woodworker will make a fine chef if she does not have any cooking talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":".  added rule 4 for clarity and updated the homebrew Charm 09-19-2019, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T11:49:03-07:00","id":1336918,"title":"","content":"Thanks for starting this thread, it's a good idea!<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that critique of the charms is welcome here as well. But if that wasn't the intent, feel free to ignore mine!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery#post1336895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Talent-Oozing Allure</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>-; <b>Mins:</b> Craft 1, Essence 1</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely like the overall effect. The one thing I'd suggest changing is bumping the minimum up to Craft 2, possibly even Craft 3. &quot;Automatically recognized as a skilled crafter&quot; seems to me like something that should require more than just novice-level crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T11:52:17-07:00","id":1336919,"title":"","content":"Here's a charm I came up with a little while ago.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Strike-Defying Command</span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins: </b>Presence 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Tiger's Dread Symmetry<br /> <br /> With a shouted command, an appeal to sympathy, or simply a stern look, a Pillar of Heaven can stop her enemy's blow. Against a single attack, this charm allows the Solar to use a defense based on ([{Appearance, Charisma, or Manipulation} + Presence + specialty]/2), rather than Parry or Evasion (for purposes of any special effects based on what type of defence is used, however, this does count as a Parry). Any intimacies the enemy has that would affect the attack also provide a bonus to the Lawgiver's defense, equal in size to the penalty they would apply to the enemy's Resolve (i.e., +1 for a Minor Intimacy, +2 for Major, and +3 for Defining). <br /> <br /> This charm is never applicable against attacks made by mindless enemies (such as zombies) or the environment.<br /> <br /> The effects of this charm depend somewhat on which social attribute the Solar invokes in her defense:<br /> <br /> Appearance-based defenses are automatically obvious to anyone watching - the Solar's anima might flare up to block the strike, or weapons simply veer aside to avoid hitting such a beautiful specimen. A physical symbol or reference to any Intimacies to be added to the defense must be stunted into the description. However, Appearance-based uses of this charm work equally well on targets who don't understand the Lawgiver's language.<br /> <br /> If the defense is Charisma-based, it takes a -2 penalty if the enemy making the attack cannot understand the Solar's language. <br /> <br /> Manipulation can be used for the defense /only/ if an appropriate Intimacy is invoked, and can <i>never</i> be used if the enemy doesn't share a language. However, if Manipulation is used, Strike-Defying Command and any Excellency used to improve the defense both gain the Mute keyword.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T12:28:17-07:00","id":1336923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1336918#post1336918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for starting this thread, it's a good idea!<br /> <br /> I'm assuming that critique of the charms is welcome here as well. But if that wasn't the intent, feel free to ignore mine!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I definitely like the overall effect. The one thing I'd suggest changing is bumping the minimum up to Craft 2, possibly even Craft 3. &quot;Automatically recognized as a skilled crafter&quot; seems to me like something that should require more than just novice-level crafting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Critique is very welcome so long as the thread doesn't get derailed into an argument about a specific Charm.<br /> <br /> Good point about the Craft requirement, I'll adjust it to 3.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1336918#post1336918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Strike-Defying Command</span></b><br /> snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Strike-Defying Command sounds fun. One thing - if you can gain a Resolve based Defense bonus, then I feel you should be able to gain an Intimacy based Defense penalty, much like how there is 1 Intimacy working for you and 1 working against you in normal Social Influence. This is really a flavor thing though, I'm not saying the Charm needs a nerf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-19-2019, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-20T06:53:51-07:00","id":1337082,"title":"","content":"I made these as a joke, but would kinda like them to work.Need some balancing since I have yet to get a feel for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Swoll Aesthetics answer or Blessed Lifting Inquiry </b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins: </b>Athletics 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Increasing strength exercise<br /> The Solar flexes his muscle into certain stances with enhances the appearances of his muscle. This will supplement any social influence roll the solar makes with [athletic] dice. This charm can be combo\u2019ed with performance charms.<br /> <br /> <b>Grand Stature Regime</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Athletics 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Swoll aesthetics answer, Triump-Forged God-Body<br /> The Solar has trained incredibly much giving her wide frame and truly wide when flexing. The solar anima can enhance this further as the solar takes a deep breath and truly tightens all her muscle fibers. As she releases this energy her body grows and expands granting the solar the legendary size merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":854,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","user":"light-hero","date":". 09-20-2019, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T08:01:18-07:00","id":1337246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1337082#post1337082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I made these as a joke, but would kinda like them to work.Need some balancing since I have yet to get a feel for that.<br /> <br /> <b>Swoll Aesthetics answer or Blessed Lifting Inquiry </b><br /> <br /> <b>Grand Stature Regime</b></div> </div> </div> </div>They look good to me. Legendary Size is more Lunar territory, but if a Solar did it that Charm would be as good a way to do it as any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T08:25:47-07:00","id":1337250,"title":"","content":"<b>Lightning Broker Technique</b><br /> <br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m; <b>Mins:</b> Bureaucracy 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Enlightened Discourse Method, Speed the Wheel<br /> <br /> The Solar can remove all apparent obstacles to a deal. Supplements a bureaucratic social influence roll, causing the any procedure, tradition or process which would prevent a deal from being brokered right there and then to be inapplicable. The Exalt might simply be so convincing that she causes the target to act rashly, or in the case of mundane obstacles she may retroactively have taken measures to remove them, such as having obtained a Vizier's permission or having completed all the necessary paperwork in advance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 09-21-2019, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T12:03:44-07:00","id":1341293,"title":"","content":"I was inspired by the recent discussion in the Ask a Question, Get an Answer thread about Solar Medicine charms, and I decided there was a hole in the charmset that could be filled:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Triply Accurate Clinician's Eye</span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- ; <b>Mins: </b>Medicine 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> <br /> So honed to the signs of illness or infirmity is the eye of a healer graced by the Unconquered Sun that merely seeing someone with such an issue is enough to awaken her instincts. As soon as she senses such a person, the Solar doctor instantly gains an instinct that they have some sort of medical issue, and a very rough sense of how severe it is (roughly broken down into &quot;mild&quot;, &quot;moderate&quot;, &quot;severe&quot;, and &quot;immediately life-threatening&quot;. More accurate assessment of the issue will require a diagnosis roll, but this charm ensures that the Copper Spider always knows <i>who</i> she must examine, and in which order.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T12:26:29-07:00","id":1341297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1337082#post1337082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Grand Stature Regime</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Athletics 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Special<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Swoll aesthetics answer, Triump-Forged God-Body<br /> The Solar has trained incredibly much giving her wide frame and truly wide when flexing. The solar anima can enhance this further as the solar takes a deep breath and truly tightens all her muscle fibers. As she releases this energy her body grows and expands granting the solar the legendary size merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd increase the cost. Lunars should be better than Solars at achieving Legendary Size, so at least the cost should be about the same. I'd also try and separate the fluff part from the actual mechanics, note down what Legendary Size even does so there's no need to cross-reference, and mention how any weird interactions with other Charms work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:21:44-07:00","id":1341326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1341293#post1341293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was inspired by the recent discussion in the Ask a Question, Get an Answer thread about Solar Medicine charms, and I decided there was a hole in the charmset that could be filled:<br /> <br /> [snip]</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's basically the Medicine equivalent of Watchman's Infallible Eye?<br /> <br /> Cool, I can dig it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T15:40:45-07:00","id":1341331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1341293#post1341293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was inspired by the recent discussion in the Ask a Question, Get an Answer thread about Solar Medicine charms, and I decided there was a hole in the charmset that could be filled:<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Triply Accurate Clinician's Eye</span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>- ; <b>Mins: </b>Medicine 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Flawless Diagnosis Technique<br /> <br /> So honed to the signs of illness or infirmity is the eye of a healer graced by the Unconquered Sun that merely seeing someone with such an issue is enough to awaken her instincts. As soon as she senses such a person, the Solar doctor instantly gains an instinct that they have some sort of medical issue, and a very rough sense of how severe it is (roughly broken down into &quot;mild&quot;, &quot;moderate&quot;, &quot;severe&quot;, and &quot;immediately life-threatening&quot;. More accurate assessment of the issue will require a diagnosis roll, but this charm ensures that the Copper Spider always knows <i>who</i> she must examine, and in which order.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on this there should be a charm that's simple, and lets you diagnose someone with a glance without touching them or talking to them. Probably Medicine 3, Essence 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T21:14:43-07:00","id":1341396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1341326#post1341326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it's basically the Medicine equivalent of Watchman's Infallible Eye?<br /> <br /> Cool, I can dig it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, that's exactly the inspiration! I was initially thinking that the character should be able to adjust the sensitivity, so to speak, to avoid being pinged every time they walk next to someone with planters warts or something, but decided that since the charm gives you details on how severe the issue is, that it should be fine. If you're not worried about people with minor medical issues, just tell the ST &quot;I'm not going to bother with those, you can just not tell me when I see them&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-14T21:46:33-07:00","id":1341400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1341396#post1341396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yup, that's exactly the inspiration! I was initially thinking that the character should be able to adjust the sensitivity, so to speak, to avoid being pinged every time they walk next to someone with planters warts or something, but decided that since the charm gives you details on how severe the issue is, that it should be fine. If you're not worried about people with minor medical issues, just tell the ST &quot;I'm not going to bother with those, you can just not tell me when I see them&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> For that kind of Charm, I usually mention in the last lines &quot;The Storyteller should not mention (X) if it is unimportant to the ongoing plot and the character's or circle's goals or Intimacies&quot;. For example, in Charms that read the intentions of all people you can perceive, since you don't really NEED the Intimacies or motives of literally everyone, just the people you wanted to read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23684-alistair","name":"Alistair","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23684_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T13:54:05-07:00","id":1345321,"title":"","content":"Something I thought of while discussing the idea of where hypnosis fits into the Abilities - I decided that Integrity needs something to help people be &quot;wise counselors&quot;, resolving others' contradictions and dilemmas. <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Sage Wisdom Dispensing Method</span></span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Integrity 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sun King Radiance <br /> <br /> Who better than the Resplendent Sun, who has already resolved the contradictions and conflicts within her own soul, to guide others to similar insight? To activate Sage Wisdom Dispensing Method, the Lawgiver must spend a scene in conversation with a target, who must voluntarily discuss a moral quandary or internal conflict he is experiencing. This counts as an automatically successful Read Intentions action on the part of the Solar to determine any relevant Intimacies the target holds. At the end of the scene, the Solar rolls (Intelligence + Integrity), with double-9s, against a difficulty of the target's Resolve+2. If successful, she may propose a new set of Intimacies for the target, that resolves his dilemma. This new set of Intimacies can involve any that the Solar knows the target holds, not just the ones he revealed in conversation. The new set should preserve the old set's targets and general orientation (either positive or negative), but can change contexts, merge or divide intimacies, and adjust strengths.<br /> <br /> <i>Example:</i> Perfect Soul has been approached by her friend Sesus Etina, who wants advice on her troubles: Etina's beloved wife, Kahina, has been revealed to her as a Lunar Anathema. During their conversation, Etina reveals to Perfect Soul that she has a Defining Intimacy of love towards Kahina, and a Major intimacy of faith to the Immaculate Faith. From other conversations, Perfect Soul knows Etina also has a Major Intimacy of loyalty to the Realm. Perfect Soul makes her roll, and proposes that Etina can resolve her conflict by adopting a new set of intimacies, that still includes a Defining love for Kahina, but changes the context of her intimacy towards the Realm to &quot;feels it is currently the best option to protect the people of Creation&quot;, and adjusting her intimacy towards the Immaculate Faith to a Minor one, with the context of &quot;thinks it is a useful support to the Realm's social stability&quot;. <br /> <br /> If the target accepts the new set of Intimacies, they immediately switch to them. This does not count as opposing their previous set of Intimacies. If the target is unwilling to switch, they count as having a Major Intimacy of respect towards the Lawgiver's wisdom, which she can use to try to persuade them to switch with social influence. If he already had such an Intimacy at the Minor or Major level, he instead counts as having it at the Defining level, while if it was already Defining, entering a decision point to contest influence based on it to change his intimacies now costs 3 wp, rather than 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-03T12:30:25-08:00","id":1345621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alistair</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1341297#post1341297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd increase the cost. Lunars should be better than Solars at achieving Legendary Size, so at least the cost should be about the same. I'd also try and separate the fluff part from the actual mechanics, note down what Legendary Size even does so there's no need to cross-reference, and mention how any weird interactions with other Charms work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I will be sure to do that, if any of my players actually wants to use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-05T14:25:41-08:00","id":1346284,"title":"","content":"Something I came up with today, just on the ground that Solar teachers should be able to very quickly teach people by demonstration.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Excellent Tutoring Demonstration Technique</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Lore 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Bridge<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> First Knowledge's Grace <i>or</i> any 3 charms from one Ability, at least one of which must require a minimum of 3 in that Ability<br /> <br /> The greatest teachers among Heaven's Lamps know that a demonstration of correct technique by the master can be more effective in instructing an apprentice than hours of theory and explanation. This charm educates a target chosen by the Solar, raising one of their Abilities to the next level, as long as this is legal. Player characters must pay for this increase out of of unspent XP, while Storyteller characters can only benefit from this charm once per story.<br /> <br /> <b>Special activation rules: </b>Excellent Tutoring Demonstration Technique can only be activated for a target after they have witnessed a demonstration of the relevant Ability by the Solar. This must involve either a successful roll that overcame a difficulty equal or higher to the dot rating the target's Ability is being raised to, or the use of a Simple or Supplemental charm with an Ability minimum of the same level. Excellent Tutoring Demonstration Technique must also be activated within a day of the target witnessing the feat. Additionally, if the Solar doesn't have First Knowledge's Grace, she may only use this charm to teach Abilities that she meets the alternate Bridge prerequisites, and in any case, she may never use the charm to raise someone's Ability higher than her own rating in it. She can only use this charm on a target once per Ability per story, but this can be reset by using Flowing Mind Prana to successfully raise their Ability. <br /> <br /> At Lore 5 and Essence 2, this charm may be repurchased, becoming capable of educating several people at once. By paying a surcharge of 5m, and WP equal to the Size of the group to be taught (as a battlegroup), she may activate Excellent Tutoring Demonstration Technique simultaneously for all targets who qualify normally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T14:58:53-08:00","id":1346587,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Preternatural Beast Union</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-; <b>Mins: </b>Wits 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Penumbra Witch Mastery, Terrestrial Circle Sorcery<br /> <br /> Perform a Sacred Hunt on a magical animal. After declaring the hunt, you must give the animal a defining positive tie to you. When you conclude this hunt, their soul becomes bonded to you and their physical form disappears in a flash of anima.<br /> <br /> While in this magical animal's Shape, your lose access to all Charms except Excellencies and Charms that would allow you to exit the Shape. Your mote pool is replaced with the animal's if it has one and you have access to all of the animal's Abilities and Merits. The animal's mote pool does not regenerate naturally and only replenishes after a full night's rest.<br /> <br /> Only 1 magical animal may be bonded to you in this way. once per Season you may release your bonded magical animal, returning it to a physical body, in order to bond a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:12:51-08:00","id":1346619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346587#post1346587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Preternatural Beast Union</span></span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> While in this magical animal's Shape, your lose access to all Charms except Excellencies and Charms that would allow you to exit the Shape.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea, but I wonder if this restriction is actually a little too harsh. There are some powerful magical creature shapes, obviously, but &quot;absolutely no charms except for Excellencies&quot; is a pretty big limit. We know that magical creatures can have Essence ratings higher than 1 (see Plentimon's Ladybug, for instance), so that might make a useful guide. Perhaps say that while in the form, your Essence is reduced by (creature's Essence +1), for purposes of which charms you can activate, and if it's effectively reduced to 0, you can only use Excellencies at that point? I think limiting an Essence 5 Lunar who's assumed the form of a Plentimon's Ladybug (Essence 2) to only Essence 2 or lower charms is a pretty good balancing mechanism.<br /> <br /> Also, I know it's not your fault, it's a matter of various things being a bit poorly defined, but there probably needs to be some kind of guideline as to what constitutes a &quot;magical beast&quot; in here. I mean, presumably a fogshark or, as mentioned, Plentimon's Ladybug, qualifies. But what about a dog of the unbroken earth? It's listed in the corebook as an elemental, so I'd guess not. But aughdeighes, from Hundred Devils Night Parade, are magical horse-shaped creatures that aren't defined. Are they elementals? Magical horses with ice and cold powers? Something else? It's weird!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T17:24:43-08:00","id":1346624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346587#post1346587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your mote pool is replaced with the animal's if it has one.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your reasoning here? It makes me leery since I think people might use it a an Excellency mote battery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T20:50:49-08:00","id":1346659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346619#post1346619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the idea, but I wonder if this restriction is actually a little too harsh. There are some powerful magical creature shapes, obviously, but &quot;absolutely no charms except for Excellencies&quot; is a pretty big limit. We know that magical creatures can have Essence ratings higher than 1 (see Plentimon's Ladybug, for instance), so that might make a useful guide. Perhaps say that while in the form, your Essence is reduced by (creature's Essence +1), for purposes of which charms you can activate, and if it's effectively reduced to 0, you can only use Excellencies at that point? I think limiting an Essence 5 Lunar who's assumed the form of a Plentimon's Ladybug (Essence 2) to only Essence 2 or lower charms is a pretty good balancing mechanism.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The general idea is that the magical animal should be used either for RP reasons or for an ability the Lunar could not get any other way, it should never be able to outshine (or heavens forbid empower) a combat Lunar.<br /> <br /> Limiting to the creature's Essence is a cool idea and it might just work. But to be perfectly honest, figuring out what exactly is balanced across all magical animals is monk's work I'm not willing to do, hence why I just closed off all Charms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346619#post1346619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I know it's not your fault, it's a matter of various things being a bit poorly defined, but there probably needs to be some kind of guideline as to what constitutes a &quot;magical beast&quot; in here. I mean, presumably a fogshark or, as mentioned, Plentimon's Ladybug, qualifies. But what about a dog of the unbroken earth? It's listed in the corebook as an elemental, so I'd guess not. But aughdeighes, from Hundred Devils Night Parade, are magical horse-shaped creatures that aren't defined. Are they elementals? Magical horses with ice and cold powers? Something else? It's weird!</div> </div> </div> </div>The devs define magical animals as literally any animal that could not possibly exist in the real world as a result of the normal evolution process. Any animal with an essence &gt; 1 or a mote pool is magical, but so are animals with supernatural abilities, such as a mouse of the Sun or a Dream Hawk. The aughdeighes specifically are not animals - you can somewhat tell from the fact they behave very strangely for animals, but the fact they have an Eclipse Charm is the real give away.<br /> <br /> There are probably edge cases beyond that (i.e. Barrow Hounds - magical animal or underworld creature?), but I'm not really sure how to solve that problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25285,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","user":"Epitome","date":". 11-07-2019, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T20:58:33-08:00","id":1346660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346624#post1346624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your reasoning here? It makes me leery since I think people might use it a an Excellency mote battery.</div> </div> </div> </div>The goal is to limit how much a Lunar can pump Excellency dice into the magical animal's native Charms, but you make a good point that it could be abused for Excellency motes. I guess I could disallow Quicksilver Second Face while in the magical animal's Shape to mitigate the worst of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-06T21:17:30-08:00","id":1346661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346659#post1346659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The devs define magical animals as literally any animal that could not possibly exist in the real world as a result of the normal evolution process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, I understand the distinction between &quot;natural animals&quot; that Lunars can turn into, and basically everything else. What I'm wondering is, what does this charm let you turn into? Is a &quot;magical beast&quot; anything that looks like an animal but has magical abilities or an essence pool? Or is it more restricted than that? <i>Does</i> this let you turn into a dog of the unbroken earth? Or a storm serpent? What about a god that happens to have an animal form? Would they qualify?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T06:01:19-08:00","id":1346704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1346661#post1346661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Right, I understand the distinction between &quot;natural animals&quot; that Lunars can turn into, and basically everything else. What I'm wondering is, what does this charm let you turn into? Is a &quot;magical beast&quot; anything that looks like an animal but has magical abilities or an essence pool? Or is it more restricted than that? <i>Does</i> this let you turn into a dog of the unbroken earth? Or a storm serpent? What about a god that happens to have an animal form? Would they qualify?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be strictly for animals that don't fall into any other category, no elemental/fair folk/god/undead. So for currently published material this would be :<ul><li>Fog Shark</li> <li>Barrow Hound (?)</li> <li>Dream Hawk</li> <li>Giant Grossbeak</li> <li>Plentimon's Ladybug</li> <li>Gem Seeker</li> <li>Gravehound</li> <li>Mouse of the Sun</li> <li>Tiger's Eye</li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:05:17-08:00","id":1351678,"title":"","content":"Here's a Lunar charm idea.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Remembrance Enshrining Practice</span></span></span></span></span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m; <b>Mins: </b>Intelligence 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Memory-Drinking Meditation<br /> <br /> The memories of the forms she takes are sacred treasures, the Lunar knows, not to be cast aside lightly. They should be preserved, to be cherished by later generations honoring the brave being that a Chosen of the Moon selected to become. This charm can only be activated while the Lunar currently has an Intimacy gained through Memory-Drinking Meditation. It allows her to create a representation of that Tie in some form. The exact form this takes can vary, but it should be something supported by an Ability the Lunar has at least three dots in. Writing a poem on the subject would require Linguistics, for example, while an interpretative dance would be Performance, and carving a statue would be Craft. <br /> <br /> Once this representation is created, the Nightwitch can use it to refresh her memory of the intimacy and thus the shape's memories. If she has eroded the Intimacy the object or activity represents, she can re-assume it (which requires re-activating Memory-Drinking Meditation as well) as part of transforming into the shape it is linked to, once again gaining access to the relevant memories. If the representation is a physical object, she must handle it and contemplate its meaning for at least a minute before transforming into the form. If it is a more transient thing, like a dance or sword kata, she must either perform it herself or watch someone else do so for at least 15 minutes before transforming. And if the representation is a written record, any accurate copy will do, but she must re-read and absorb the meaning of the text for at least an hour before the transformation.<br /> <br /> Recording someone's memories in this manner means that, for better or worse, they are no longer completely private (either to the Lunar or the person whose shape was stolen). Someone else who sees or otherwise experiences the representation can interpret it and learn about the form's memories. Basic interpretation calls for an (Intelligence + [Ability the representation was made with]) roll of difficulty 1. If successful, the viewer can then use a Read Intentions action to determine the Intimacy the representation is tied to (using the Lunar's Guile as the target, with the usual -2 penalty for thinking they are unobserved). If the interpretation roll achieves at least 3 successes, the viewer also gains a broad idea of the contents of the memories tied to the representation (for example, &quot;This dance represents the memories of a soldier regarding her commanding officer&quot;). With 5 or more successes, the contents of the memories are revealed in more depth, as if the original memory holder was truthfully describing their own recollections. <br /> <br /> If another Lunar gains access to the same shape, and also has Memory-Drinking Meditation, he can use a representation created with Remembrance Enshrining Practice to assume the Intimacy and memories associated with it in the same way the original creator can.<br /> <br /> If the Lunar knows the Intelligence 5, Essence 3 repurchase of Memory-Drinking Meditation, she can choose when creating a representation whether it includes only the memories directly associated with the Intimacy, or the shape's complete memories. If she chooses the former, when re-assuming the Intimacy she only gains the more limited set of memories, and does not have the option to pay Memory-Drinking Meditation's surcharge. If she chooses to encode the shape's full memories, she can pay the surcharge later and re-assume all their memories. However, a representation that contains the target's complete memories can be read by others for all their recollections, making it more of a risk to create such a representation. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T12:14:43-08:00","id":1352196,"title":"","content":"There is a Solar War Charm here, I an just not seeing the stats yet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T12:43:31-08:00","id":1352202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1352196#post1352196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a Solar War Charm here, I an just not seeing the stats yet.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oimIMZHNRVI</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which effect are you thinking of here? 'Cause I can see at least two Solar-level War effects going on - getting a bunch of naked soldiers with no armor to charge headlong into a prepared wall of spears without flinching, and still keep formation and discipline even when the first five or six ranks have been utterly decimated; <i>and</i> preparing a group of spearmen so that they stand totally firm and just completely slaughter a group charging at them, never breaking ranks or even a single one getting tired or panicking or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T13:40:43-08:00","id":1352209,"title":"","content":"Well the naked warriors running into their deaths would a charm that applies perfect morale (is that not a thing already)?<br /> <br /> The spear wall might be a strategem thing or some special battle group attack... then one could apply a charm.<br /> <br /> <br /> Atleast that is how far I have gotten.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T14:49:20-08:00","id":1352225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1352209#post1352209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the naked warriors running into their deaths would a charm that applies perfect morale (is that not a thing already)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, perfect morale is one of the things Tiger Warrior Training Technique can give (at Essence 3). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>light-hero</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The spear wall might be a strategem thing or some special battle group attack... then one could apply a charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a stratagem, I'd describe it as follows:<br /> <br /> <b>Spear-Wall (<i>threshold</i>: 2): </b>The victorious general arranges her forces on the battlefield such that a crucial strategic point is commanded by one of her units, which is braced to block a charge. To implement this stratagem, the commander must have access to a battlegroup armed with spears, great swords, poleaxes, or similar weapons that can be braced effectively. If the spear-wall stratagem is implemented successfully, to win the battle the opposing general must eliminate the affected battlegroup. The battlegroup in spear-wall formation receives a +2 non-charm bonus to its Defense against ranged attacks, and automatically reduces the Magnitude damage taken from successful attacks by 1. Melee attacks against the battlegroup are automatically treated as clashes, without the battlegroup needing to declare a delay or spend initiative, and the battlegroup in spear-wall formation receives +2 non-charm dice on such clashes. <br /> <br /> The benefits of spear-wall formation persist for the affected battlegroup until it loses a melee clash, or until it loses a dot of Size from magnitude loss or fails a rout check for any reason. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T00:10:28-08:00","id":1353267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1352225#post1352225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Spear-Wall (<i>threshold</i>: 2): </b>The victorious general arranges her forces on the battlefield such that a crucial strategic point is commanded by one of her units, which is braced to block a charge. To implement this stratagem, the commander must have access to a battlegroup armed with spears, great swords, poleaxes, or similar weapons that can be braced effectively. If the spear-wall stratagem is implemented successfully, to win the battle the opposing general must eliminate the affected battlegroup. The battlegroup in spear-wall formation receives a +2 non-charm bonus to its Defense against ranged attacks, and automatically reduces the Magnitude damage taken from successful attacks by 1. Melee attacks against the battlegroup are automatically treated as clashes, without the battlegroup needing to declare a delay or spend initiative, and the battlegroup in spear-wall formation receives +2 non-charm dice on such clashes.<br /> <br /> The benefits of spear-wall formation persist for the affected battlegroup until it loses a melee clash, or until it loses a dot of Size from magnitude loss or fails a rout check for any reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is great attempt at making a strategem. <br /> <br /> Where we might differ is that would not give the defense bonus or demand that the battlegroup must be defeated. Here I owe some kind of replacement. But I very much thankful for this idea. I have an idea with reach and rangeband. Or maybe hazards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:38:34-07:00","id":1415547,"title":"","content":"Rise! Riiiiiissseee!<br /> <br /> So a couple of my PCs have approached me with requests for custom homebrew Dragon-Blooded Charms. I didn't really want to make a whole new thread for two Charms, but I really... am not sure about whether these are suitably balanced for Dragon-Blooded PCs. I'd love feedback from folks with more 3E experience than me (and anyone else who care's to comment).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Charm number 1</b></u><br /> <br /> The idea here was that PC 1 wanted a Dragon-Blooded equivilant to Celestial Bliss Trick (Performance Charm, Core Page 368), and they presented the &quot;base&quot; Charm below as an Earth aspected Charm. It didn't feel &quot;Earth&quot; themed to me, so I changed it to Wood and drafted some elemental varients.<br /> <br /> <b>Earthly Pleasure Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 1WP; <b>Mins:</b> Performance 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Wood, Balanced, Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> (Essence Weeks)<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Enticing Paramour Passion<br /> <br /> The Exalt draws on the primal Essence that underpins human sensuality, and channels it upon a lover in an intense act of lovemaking. In the afterglow, the Exalt may automatically Inspire the emotion of their choice in their lover. This inflamed passion lasts until the end of the scene, and the Dragon-Blooded gains (Essence) dice to social influence actions targeting her lover for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Thereafter, whenever their lover becomes aware of the physical presence of the Dragon-Blooded whilst this Charm is active, the Dragon-Blooded may Reflexively roll (Appearance + Performance) with (Essence) automatic successes to Inspire that same emotion again.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3, elemental variants of this Charm may be purchased for 3XP each:<br /> <br /> <b>Air: </b>The Dragon-Blooded need not be physically present to re-Inspire the chosen emotion, instead inflaming passions anew by sending written social influence or by sending a gift to their lover.<br /> <b>Earth: </b>As the Air variant, save passions are re-inflamed when the lover is in the presence of one of the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s subordinates in a Bureaucratic organization or when inside a building strongly associated with the Dragon-Blooded (such as a manse they are attuned to, or the headquarters of an organization they belong to).<br /> <b>Fire: </b>Fire\u2019s passions burn hottest of all. The Dragon-Blooded may use the inflamed passion to enable Life-Changing Tasks with Persuade actions (though it otherwise only counts as a Major Intimacy, for example for the purposes of modifying Resolve).<br /> <b>Water: </b>Few things are as fluid as human emotions. Every time the Dragon-Blooded overcomes their lover\u2019s Resolve to successfully Inspire an emotion, they may spend a point of Willpower to change which emotion this Charm Inspires.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Charm Number 2</b></u><br /> <br /> PC 2 has the Orichalcum Powerbow Summer Thunder. She's a Ride based archer who has been deprived of her enormous dinosaur mount... more than once. The suggestion is simple: Phantom Steed as an Evocation of Summer Thunder. Summon a ghostly echo of Hiparkes, prerequisite charm being Squadron-Inspiring Flare, Charm being identical in all ways to the Solar Ride Charm of the same name (Core Page 383).<br /> <br /> I'm fairly... okay with that? But my question is whether it should allow her to purchase Evoke the Equestrian Echo, and whether folks think I should nerf Evoke the Equestrian Echo because, you know, it's clearly meant for Solars (or whether the fact that Solars get the Resonant bonus but a DB wielder won't is a big enough nerf)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-26-2020, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T08:46:56-07:00","id":1415554,"title":"","content":"For charm number 2 ... I'd say no on the basis of theme. Making Glorious Solar Whatsits is one of the Solar themes, that Solar Essence transcends the need for tools. (Boats, Horses, Swords, etc). I'd probably have a theoretical DB ride charm that brought in a mount involve shaping it from raw Elements, almost like summoning an Elemental. So thematically, I'd probably refluff it to involve the Elements, and tie it to the aura and anima. Maybe spend anima or need an appropriately impressive elemental source. Mechanically, I don't see a problem with a way for her to get a mount via the bow. But I'd probably look at her Ride charms, and actually make it an appropriate DB charm instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","user":"Scrollreader","date":". 09-26-2020, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26421-scrollreader","name":"Scrollreader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26421_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T09:43:46-07:00","id":1415564,"title":"","content":"I wish to god that there was a list that let you have guidelines on how long it took to make something.<br /> <br /> *checks the book* <br /> <br /> Ok that's it. I hate this, and this is probably going to be broken. But I don't care. <br /> <br /> Elemental Harmony Transformation<br /> Essence 4, Craft 5<br /> Prereqs: Shaping Hand Style<br /> <br /> Gaia is a Harmony of many elements. Many types, all working to the same goal of maintaining Creation. And thus the same way Dragonblooded can harmonize themselves in teamwork and cooperation. The DB divides the time to create superior projects like artifact making or crafting palaces by his Essence. With each Dragonblooded that joins him in crafting (with the required prerequisite ability dots), he can increase the time division by1, up to his (Essence). Up to (Essence) Dbs can assist him. Only one worker needs to know the cahrm. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-26T10:20:20-07:00","id":1415569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415564#post1415564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish to god that there was a list that let you have guidelines on how long it took to make something.<br /> <br /> *checks the book*<br /> <br /> Ok that's it. I hate this, and this is probably going to be broken. But I don't care.<br /> <br /> Elemental Harmony Transformation<br /> Essence 4, Craft 5<br /> Prereqs: Shaping Hand Style<br /> <br /> Gaia is a Harmony of many elements. Many types, all working to the same goal of maintaining Creation. And thus the same way Dragonblooded can harmonize themselves in teamwork and cooperation. The DB divides the time to create superior projects like artifact making or crafting palaces by his Essence. With each Dragonblooded that joins him in crafting (with the required prerequisite ability dots), he can increase the time division by1, up to his (Essence). Up to (Essence) Dbs can assist him. Only one worker needs to know the cahrm.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Real quick:<br /> <br /> So my Essence 5 DB can divine Superior Craft times by 5? Then with five other helpers, she can divide those times by 10 instead?<br /> <br /> <s>I don't have time to check the Solar Charms, but how does that compare? Offhand, it seems really fast.<br /> <br /> Probably better to just base it off the number of Dragon-Blooded: so with five helpers, you divide the time by five not 10.<br /> <br /> And as it's an Essence 4 Charm, I'd probably just let upto five Dragon-Blooded assist rather than 4 or 5 (my way is a little incongruous with game design, but it's easier to actually play).</s><br /> <br /> [Edit]<br /> <br /> Check page 241 for artifact craft times.<br /> <br /> And also, ignore my initial opinion above. It still seems significantly slower than Thousand Forge Hands (about par for artifact 3 items).<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it, why not copy Thousand Forge Hands, but use number of Dragon-Blooded helpers instead of (Essence) (keep the max number of helpers capped at Essence) and have it at Superior Projects take (6 - helpers) months to complete?<br /> <br /> [Edit edit]<br /> <br /> How about this?<br /> <br /> Elemental Harmony Transformation<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prereqs: Forge-Hand Prana<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are greater than the sum of their parts and the Essence of a thousand craftsmen flows between them. United, their power is legion and their well is bottomless. <br /> <br /> When she creates a superior slot, she may use this Charm to nominate upto (Essence) Dragon-Blooded as her Companions to assist with the project. This greatly speeds her efforts to begin the project (p. 239), though each Companion working on the project must meet the prequisites to start the project on their own (they need not know this Charm).<br /> <br /> This Charm guarantees that the design and forging work that comes before she can roll to finish takes no longer than ([Artifact Rating + 2] - Companion) months (minimum 1 week) for two to four dot Artifacts, and no more than (5 - Companion) years (minimum 6 months) for Artifact 5.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial's Sworn Kin do not have to meet the trait minimums for the project, provided they can Stunt how their expertise can be used to assist in the project.<br /> <br /> This Charm may not be used on Legendary projects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-27-2020, 03:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T12:39:37-07:00","id":1415718,"title":"","content":"Solar melee charm to use shields better<br /> <br /> <br /> Wings of Mars<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dipping Swallow Defense, Excellent Strike<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Shields are exceptional weapons to control the enemy on battle. The Lawgiver has learned to blend flexible defense and overbearing control above and beyond her peers on the battlefield.</i><br /> <br /> Pick 3 benefits to use armed with a shield. Others can be bought for 2xp each.<br /> <br /> 1) The shield loses its -2 damage penalty.<br /> <br /> 2) Full Defenses with the shield no longer cost 1i, and can be done in crash.<br /> <br /> 3) Full Defenses can be flurried without a defense penalty.<br /> <br /> 4) Clashes with the shield benefit from the +2 bonus of a 2-handed weapon.<br /> <br /> 5) For 2m, you may flurry Full Defense with any action that can normally be placed in a flurry.<br /> <br /> 6) Essence reinforces the shield and resonates back onto the Solar, adding 1 Hardness and [Essence] to her armored soak against attacks that hit through her Parry. If the solar is unarmored the bonuses increase by 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-27T14:11:02-07:00","id":1415735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415547#post1415547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rise! Riiiiiissseee!<br /> <br /> So a couple of my PCs have approached me with requests for custom homebrew Dragon-Blooded Charms. I didn't really want to make a whole new thread for two Charms, but I really... am not sure about whether these are suitably balanced for Dragon-Blooded PCs. I'd love feedback from folks with more 3E experience than me (and anyone else who care's to comment).</div> </div> </div> </div> Nice \u2013 some thoughts if of interest\u2026<br /> <br /> Charm No.1<br /> <br /> As written (and going by the Water variant), this could be used to instil revulsion, shame etc, no? Is that the intent? I <i>shudder</i> to think what your players will use it for if so\u2026<br /> <br /> Comparing it to, say, Haunting Words Infliction, I\u2019d maybe say it could do with being E3 and a mote or two more expensive, but those are quibbles. The Earth variant feels a little off to me \u2013 maybe have it work by hearing stories/witnessing examples of the user\u2019s inspirational and unflagging resolve?<br /> <br /> Charm No.2<br /> <br /> Is Evoke The Equestrian Echo really that much better than Dragon\u2019s Egg Hatched to worry overly about this, especially if the player has had to suck up not getting much mileage from their survival/ride charms previously? At E3 with DEH you can summon an Elite Trooper with Centaur and Deadly Weaponry merits for 4m and 1a less (admittedly spending a WP dot and needing a source) than EtEE that lasts for days (that you could enhance via Elemental Bond Meditation). If you and your players are happy with it, then surely what you're planning is A-OK.<br /> <br /> Arguably DEH (with some fiddling/tweaks to suit your player as, if I remember right, Melody\u2019s not much of an Occultist) could serve the purpose of both Phantom Steed and EtEE.<br /> <br /> But the lack of resonance seems nerf enough to me at least if you'd rather just stick with Phantom Steed &gt; EtEE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T10:47:32-07:00","id":1415851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415569#post1415569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Check page 241 for artifact craft times.<br /> <br /> And also, ignore my initial opinion above. It still seems significantly slower than Thousand Forge Hands (about par for artifact 3 items).<br /> <br /> Actually, thinking about it, why not copy Thousand Forge Hands, but use number of Dragon-Blooded helpers instead of (Essence) (keep the max number of helpers capped at Essence) and have it at Superior Projects take (6 - helpers) months to complete?<br /> <br /> [Edit edit]<br /> <br /> How about this?<br /> <br /> Elemental Harmony Transformation<br /> Cost: 10m, 1wp; Mins: Craft 5, Essence 4<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prereqs: Forge-Hand Prana<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial Exalted are greater than the sum of their parts and the Essence of a thousand craftsmen flows between them. United, their power is legion and their well is bottomless.<br /> <br /> When she creates a superior slot, she may use this Charm to nominate upto (Essence) Dragon-Blooded as her Companions to assist with the project. This greatly speeds her efforts to begin the project (p. 239), though each Companion working on the project must meet the prequisites to start the project on their own (they need not know this Charm).<br /> <br /> This Charm guarantees that the design and forging work that comes before she can roll to finish takes no longer than ([Artifact Rating + 2] - Companion) months (minimum 1 week) for two to four dot Artifacts, and no more than (5 - Companion) years (minimum 6 months) for Artifact 5.<br /> <br /> The Terrestrial's Sworn Kin do not have to meet the trait minimums for the project, provided they can Stunt how their expertise can be used to assist in the project.<br /> <br /> This Charm may not be used on Legendary projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. Yes, that is a lot more smoother than before. <br /> <br /> My fear is that it may be *too* powerful for Dragonblooded. As much as I like them, Dragonblooded are meant to be weaker than Solar. Not as week as some books made them out to be (fuck you, 2e), but still, weaker. Since there are probably 100 Dragonblooded to every member of the Celestial Host, I sort of want to limit their powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T01:37:41-07:00","id":1415951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415851#post1415851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. Yes, that is a lot more smoother than before. <br /> <br /> My fear is that it may be *too* powerful for Dragonblooded. As much as I like them, Dragonblooded are meant to be weaker than Solar. Not as week as some books made them out to be (fuck you, 2e), but still, weaker. Since there are probably 100 Dragonblooded to every member of the Celestial Host, I sort of want to limit their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Solar Charm, Thousand Forge Hands, reduces artifact 2-4 to (6-Essence) weeks (this is months) and Artifact 5 to months (this is years), is available at Essence 2 (this is Essence 4, and DBs don't have Supernal), doesn't require teamwork from skilled artisans (this does), and can be used on Legendary projects (this can't).<br /> <br /> DBs shouldn't be able to make Artifact N/As, and this Charm doesn't change that. Artifact 5 should be a massive endeavour: this Charm requires three DBs working together to guarentee the normal 2 year minimum for Artifact 5, four DBs to cut the Crafting time in half, and Essence 5 and five DBs to get this to six months where a Solar can do it in one month on her own.<br /> <br /> Plus DBs can't just crap out Craft points like Solars, and are pretty effectively gatekept out of First Age Artifice due to a lack of White Points. I think it scans.<br /> <br /> But you could force the contributing Companion Crafters to pay Gold Points to make the Superior Slot and/or make them pay on the finishing rolls if you wanted to handicap it further. Or make it only applicable to Jade artifacts. Or borrow from Savant and Sorcerer and say the resulting artifact has to be oversized and bulky. Or just bump the Craft times up.<br /> <br /> Your original idea is fine. But it means DBs will be twice as fast as Solars at making Artifact 2 (four times as fast for Jade artifacts if it stacks with Forge Hand Prana), about the same for Artifact 3, slower for Artifact 4 and much slower for Artifact 5. Which might fit perfectly with your homebrew DB/Alchemical set-up because Artifact 2s will be WAAAY more common (as your hundreds of DBs will be better than Solars at making them) but Artifact 4-5 will stay rare. But for an actual default game, I'd rather the PCs invest in one or two powerful artifacts than equip their followers with excess weak artifacts. And too many cheap Artifact 2s risks tipping that White Point balance -- I think it's better to incentivise PCs to go for quality over quantity.<br /> <br /> Also, the 1E Alchemicals book had rules for making Autochothon-Akuma that might be useful for you if you were looking to boost DB crafting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 09-29-2020, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T08:39:49-07:00","id":1415985,"title":"","content":"Additionally, looking at the statistics for crafting artifacts as a DB, no matter how much you minmax you can't get much more than a 40% chance to finish an artifact 5 until you reach Essence 5.<br /> <br /> You can count on the fingers of one hand the number of DBs in all of Creation that both reach E5 and are top tier crafters. There's a reason a major power like lookshy <i>can't </i>do maintenance to keep their entire arsenal functioning at peak performance. The people needed simply don't exist.<br /> <br /> And on anyone other than these guys...who will spend half a decade and resources to bankrupt a small country on the low chance that you might get a new sword and a high chance it just breaks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T09:11:09-07:00","id":1415989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415735#post1415735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Nice \u2013 some thoughts if of interest\u2026<br /> <br /> Charm No.1<br /> <br /> As written (and going by the Water variant), this could be used to instil revulsion, shame etc, no? Is that the intent? I <i>shudder</i> to think what your players will use it for if so\u2026<br /> <br /> Comparing it to, say, Haunting Words Infliction, I\u2019d maybe say it could do with being E3 and a mote or two more expensive, but those are quibbles. The Earth variant feels a little off to me \u2013 maybe have it work by hearing stories/witnessing examples of the user\u2019s inspirational and unflagging resolve?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was <u><i>exactly</i></u> the intent, but on review it's probably too powerful.<br /> <br /> (Haunting Words Infliction is Instant duration, so the motes aren't committed. But I'm looking at Impeccable Purity Lavation and I agree this is undercosted.)<br /> <br /> Second Draft:<br /> <br /> <b>Earthly Pleasure Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5m, 1WP; <b>Mins:</b> Performance 4, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Wood, Balanced, Mute<br /> <b>Duration:</b> (Essence Weeks)<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Enticing Paramour Passion<br /> <br /> The Exalt draws on the primal Essence that underpins human sensuality, and channels it upon a lover in an intense act of lovemaking. In the afterglow, the Exalt may automatically Inspire an emotion of love or lust (or a similiar passion) in their lover. This inflamed passion lasts until the end of the scene, and the Dragon-Blooded gains (Essence) dice to social influence actions targeting her lover for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Thereafter, whenever their lover becomes aware of the physical presence of the Dragon-Blooded whilst this Charm is active, the Dragon-Blooded may Reflexively roll (Appearance + Performance) with (Essence) automatic successes to Inspire that same emotion again.<br /> <br /> Elemental variants of this Charm may be purchased for 3XP each:<br /> <br /> <b>Air: </b>The Dragon-Blooded need not be physically present to re-Inspire the chosen emotion, instead inflaming passions anew by sending written social influence to their lover, or using long distance communication Charms like Wind-Carried Words Technique.<br /> <b>Earth: </b>As the Air variant, save passions are re-inflamed when the lover is sent an object Crafted by the Dragon-Blooded, or uses such a gift to achieve something significant in the scene (such as using a sword forged by the Dragon-Blooded to defeat a non-trivial opponent in combat).<br /> <b>Fire: </b>Fire\u2019s passions burn hottest of all. The Dragon-Blooded may use the inflamed passion to enable Life-Changing Tasks with Persuade actions (though it otherwise only counts as a Major Intimacy, for example for the purposes of modifying Resolve).<br /> <b>Water: </b>Few things are as fluid as human emotions. The Dragon-Blooded may Inspire the emotion of their choice rather than love or lust (Inspiring revolution, hatred, sadness, joy or any other feeling they wish). When successfully rolling to re-Inspire the chosen emotion, they may also activate Passion-Transmuting Nuance as a Reflexive Charm, if they know it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415735#post1415735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Charm No.2<br /> <br /> Is Evoke The Equestrian Echo really that much better than Dragon\u2019s Egg Hatched to worry overly about this, especially if the player has had to suck up not getting much mileage from their survival/ride charms previously? At E3 with DEH you can summon an Elite Trooper with Centaur and Deadly Weaponry merits for 4m and 1a less (admittedly spending a WP dot and needing a source) than EtEE that lasts for days (that you could enhance via Elemental Bond Meditation). If you and your players are happy with it, then surely what you're planning is A-OK.<br /> <br /> Arguably DEH (with some fiddling/tweaks to suit your player as, if I remember right, Melody\u2019s not much of an Occultist) could serve the purpose of both Phantom Steed and EtEE.<br /> <br /> But the lack of resonance seems nerf enough to me at least if you'd rather just stick with Phantom Steed &gt; EtEE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Melody is Occult 0. Buying upto Occult 5 and branching into Reya's area of Speciality is probably not a great start.<br /> <br /> How do you feel about just porting DEH to Surivival? I mean, I get why it's in Occult, but I'm looking at the Survival Fire Signature Charm (tame wildfires, and use them to track down your enemies) and it doesn't feel incongruous to me to just make it a Survival Charm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T09:25:12-07:00","id":1415993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415985#post1415985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additionally, looking at the statistics for crafting artifacts as a DB, no matter how much you minmax you can't get much more than a 40% chance to finish an artifact 5 until you reach Essence 5.<br /> <br /> You can count on the fingers of one hand the number of DBs in all of Creation that both reach E5 and are top tier crafters. There's a reason a major power like lookshy <i>can't </i>do maintenance to keep their entire arsenal functioning at peak performance. The people needed simply don't exist.<br /> <br /> And on anyone other than these guys...who will spend half a decade and resources to bankrupt a small country on the low chance that you might get a new sword and a high chance it just breaks?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415718#post1415718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar melee charm to use shields better<br /> <br /> <br /> Wings of Mars<br /> Cost: \u2014; Mins: Melee 2, Essence 1<br /> Type: Permanent<br /> Keywords: None<br /> Duration: Permanent<br /> Prerequisite Charms: Dipping Swallow Defense, Excellent Strike</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks good. My only proviso would be making number 6 not stack with things like Invulnerable Skin of Bronze or other effects that add (Essence) to Soak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T10:27:23-07:00","id":1416011,"title":"","content":"Dragonblooded teamwork charms! <br /> <br /> Encompassing Flame Enhancement<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Melee 4, Essence 4<br /> The Dragonblooded are the flame, and Darkness, fears them. With a gesture, the Dragonblooded and his compatriot's weapon explodes into flame or glows red. The number of people who can benefit from this charm range from Essence X 3. Damage turns into lethal as clubs turn red-hot, and lethal weapons gain the piercing tag. All weapons gain the stats of heavy weaponry. Whenever these weapons strike an enemy, there is a one-time environmental hazard of a bonfire. <br /> <br /> Wind-carried thoughts whirlwind<br /> Cost: 4m (+1 per person)<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Lore 3, Essence 2<br /> The scions of Mela are of the air, all-encompassing, all connecting, and are the breath which carries words and thoughts between minds. Only one Dragonblooded is needed for this charm to work. The Dragonblooded can add up to Essence X 2 to the group. In this group, all thoughts and minds come together in harmony and coordination, like clockwork. There is no language barrier no cultural gap. In this state, the group can carry out any kind of group intellectual activity, from decoding a cipher, writing up laws for a new industry, or planning out a 5 year plan. At the end of a planning session, the group rolls their entire combined pool against the difficulty of the plan, instead of the main leader and assistants. <br /> <br /> A/N: Oh god where is the bureaucracy system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T00:12:51-07:00","id":1416067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416011#post1416011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dragonblooded teamwork charms! <br /> <br /> Encompassing Flame Enhancement<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Melee 4, Essence 4<br /> The Dragonblooded are the flame, and Darkness, fears them. With a gesture, the Dragonblooded and his compatriot's weapon explodes into flame or glows red. The number of people who can benefit from this charm range from Essence X 3. Damage turns into lethal as clubs turn red-hot, and lethal weapons gain the piercing tag. All weapons gain the stats of heavy weaponry. Whenever these weapons strike an enemy, there is a one-time environmental hazard of a bonfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great idea. WAAAAY too cheap.<br /> <br /> I'd make it 6m, Duration: Aura and require a source of flame.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wind-carried thoughts whirlwind<br /> Cost: 4m (+1 per person)<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Lore 3, Essence 2<br /> The scions of Mela are of the air, all-encompassing, all connecting, and are the breath which carries words and thoughts between minds. Only one Dragonblooded is needed for this charm to work. The Dragonblooded can add up to Essence X 2 to the group. In this group, all thoughts and minds come together in harmony and coordination, like clockwork. There is no language barrier no cultural gap. In this state, the group can carry out any kind of group intellectual activity, from decoding a cipher, writing up laws for a new industry, or planning out a 5 year plan. At the end of a planning session, the group rolls their entire combined pool against the difficulty of the plan, instead of the main leader and assistants. </div> </div> </div>Not sure what the intended interaction with dice pool limits is. Or the advantage over Speech Without Words/With One Mind. Or why it's in Lore rather than Linguistics or Bureaucracy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A/N: Oh god where is the bureaucracy system? </div> </div> </div>No-one wants to play Bureaucrat: The Stampening.<br /> <br /> If you must make a roll, then the ST says the difficulty and goal number as any standard extended roll. But the Projects System basically just assumes you automatically succeed at whatever standard bureaucratic project you oversee offscreen, barring appropriate dramatic complications which you have to play out how you resolve.<br /> <br /> RAW a super Bureaucracy Charm like this does nothing (or, at least, very little). But, again, if It's for your novel don't worry about it. Planning projects together is very on-theme for DBs, and the concept behind being able to work together supernaturally well on intellectual/social pursuits is sound.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T01:12:12-07:00","id":1416075,"title":"","content":"Yeah, sorry if it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> It's just that I see the 2nd edition terrestrial Excellency, and think 'this is fucking awesome'. Terrestrial should be the greatest officers ever made, taking groups of mortals and turning them into greater than the sum of their parts. <br /> <br /> And as for the charm... Isn't the dB literally the source of the fire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T03:04:09-07:00","id":1416087,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415989#post1415989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Earthly Pleasure Prana</b></div> </div> </div> </div></span><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">V. cool. Looking forward to </span><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Danireya and Ganan both learning this charm and using it on each other. Can only end well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1415989#post1415989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Yeah, Melody is Occult 0. Buying up to Occult 5 and branching into Reya's area of Speciality is probably not a great start.<br /> <br /> How do you feel about just porting DEH to Surivival? I mean, I get why it's in Occult, but I'm looking at the Survival Fire Signature Charm (tame wildfires, and use them to track down your enemies) and it doesn't feel incongruous to me to just make it a Survival Charm.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be more than happy with that at my table for what it's worth, as you say there's defo some crossover for it in other Survival charms.<br /> <br /> Will add though that my main intention was noting that your original plan for Phantom Steed etc isn't really any more potent than other similar charms DBs have available to them, and if Melody's player is keen to emphasise building on her mastery of Summer Thunder then that seems appropriate \u2013 claiming the orichalcum bow of a defeated Ananthema is a pretty big deal for the character I'd say. If that's what they want to do I reckon go for it.<br /> <br /> But I have a big ol\u2019 soft spot for DEH (even though I hope it's tweaked some before release) \u2013 I think it's an interesting and fun idea, so if of use outside of a straight port here's a starter for 10 proposal for an adapted charm for Melody that can be ignored/refined at your leisure, as well as, well... some further ideas on a charm re-purchase that should probably just get in the sea.<br /> <br /> (I chose three lower-powered animals from Core as I didn't want to have to steer people to Lunars for stats, but the chosen options can definitely stand tweaking. I assumed she'd want a horse to get some mileage out of her Ride charms).<br /> <br /> <b>The Dragon Summons Their Court</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1a, 1wp; Mins: Survival 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> (Essence + Wits) days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Animal Empathy Technique, Wild-Wandering Forester's Charm<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood draws upon the elemental forces that course through Creation's wilderness, cultivating raw essence into the form of a bestial servant.<br /> <br /> This charm functions in identical fashion to Dragon's Egg Hatched, with the following exception:<br /> <br /> - The base traits of the created elemental are either those of a wolf, horse or raiton (Exalted, pp. 562, 567, 570).<br /> <br /> <u><b>Work in progress, not very well thought through and far too clunky potential addition that's probably not worth bothering with (i.e. just use the charm as written above)...</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>(but, but, Pokemon...)</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> - If the Dragon-Blood also knows Elemental Bond Meditation, an Essence 4 repurchase of The Dragon Summons Their Court allows the Dragon-Blood to train an elemental created by this charm, representing the Dragon-Blood refining their skill at shaping raw essence into a more potent form through meditation and practise. The following additional rules now apply:<br /> <br /> - The cost to summon an elemental that has received ANY training is increased to 8m. The Dragon-Blood can only create ONE trained elemental at any one time. The Dragon-Blood can still elect to create a \u2018normal\u2019 elemental of any base type or element that has not received any training for the original cost listed above and can create and maintain as many of these as their mote pool, willpower and anima resources allow.<br /> <br /> - A trained elemental always carries over its consciousness, personality, memories, and Intimacies each time it is created.<br /> <br /> - Training a created elemental requires specialties in Occult (Elementals) and a Survival specialty specific to the base type of elemental being created, animal husbandry for a wolf or horse and falconry for a raiton.<br /> <br /> - Any training that is undertaken applies ONLY to an elemental of the same base type AND element that has received said training. For example, a Dragon-Blood creates a wolf-based Wood elemental and trains it to use the unhorse gambit. The Dragon-Blood is now able to summon one wolf Wood elemental trained in the unhorse gambit in addition to any number of untrained wolf, horse or raiton elementals of any element at any one time. Later, the same Dragon-Blood creates a wolf Air elemental and trains it to use the distract gambit and the disarm gambit. The Dragon-Blood can now create a wolf Wood elemental trained in the unhorse gambit OR a wolf Air elemental trained in the district and disarm gambit in addition to any number of untrained wolf, horse or raiton elementals of any element at any one time.<br /> <br /> - The number of trained elementals a Dragon-Blood knows how to create is limited to her Essence.<br /> <br /> - Training a created elemental functions exactly as described in Exalted, pp. 554 with the additional caveats that the difficulty to train a created elemental is always difficulty 4 (reflecting the deep focus and discipline required of the Dragon-Blood to shape the elements and infuse it with knowledge each time she fashions an elemental); the Dragon-Blood does not receive any bonus dice for Intimacies; the elemental must be created in order to receive training but any successes rolled carry over each time an elemental of the same base type and element is created, albeit fading at the usual rate if the specific elemental being trained is not created again within two or three days. Any relevant charms can be used to enhance the training of the elemental in the usual way.<br /> <br /> - Should a trained elemental created by this charm be destroyed, the Dragon-Blood who created them suffers one automatic health level of bashing damage, but othewise there is no effect and nothing to stop the Dragon-Blood from creating another example of a trained elemental of the same type later on.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 09-30-2020, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-30T05:33:08-07:00","id":1416091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416075#post1416075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And as for the charm... Isn't the dB literally the source of the fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Then it should probably cost a level of anima or something.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> Moss, cool ideas, I'll talk it over with the players next session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-01T12:53:13-07:00","id":1416323,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a gourd. Like Suika's endless gourd of wine. <br /> <br /> At lower levels, it simply gives good wine. Resource 4 worth of any kind of liquid inside of it, whether its Fire Beer, Honeywine, or any other kind of valuable alcohol. Maybe its water, or maybe its delicious soup (ignore how the small spout can spew out meat chunks). Either way, delicious, tasty, and pretty useful in any situation where supplies are hard to get. <br /> <br /> At higher levels things get funky. The stuff it spits out turns magical. Water you drink from it lets you go for days without drinking again. Good, if bog-standard alcohol turns into Celestial Wine. You can spew out alchemical products using this. You can use this gourd to throw out water-bending attacks, like using it to create oil slicks or sprays of deadly caustic poison. <br /> <br /> At even higher levels things go crazy. Your gourd can supply an entire city with wine, synchronising with every single wine cup to make sure that they never go empty, letting the entire city party for days on end. Your gourd doesn't just spit out deadly burning oil or wine that the gods will fight to drink; it can also spit out storm clouds, hurricanes, or sandstorms, capable of turning armies, cities, and entire kingdoms to deadly ash as you drink and make merry atop of their charred corpses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T14:59:16-07:00","id":1416645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416075#post1416075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, sorry if it doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> It's just that I see the 2nd edition terrestrial Excellency, and think 'this is fucking awesome'. Terrestrial should be the greatest officers ever made, taking groups of mortals and turning them into greater than the sum of their parts.<br /> <br /> And as for the charm... Isn't the dB literally the source of the fire?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the idea behind Encompassing Flame Enhancement but agree with John it\u2019s waaaay too potent for its cost. Also, few quibbles on things as written, e.g. the heavy weapon stats thing, as a player/ST I\u2019d take that to mean ALL stats are swapped \u2013 so medium weapons lose their parry bonus, light weapons lose their accuracy etc, which doesn\u2019t seem the intention, and do already piercing weapons not gain any benefit?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d potentially instead look to do something like giving a group super-charged benefits of the Fire-aspected Dragon-Graced Weapon (say +3 Overwhelming or something) plus the environmental bonus as an alternative, costing the DB anima. But, to reiterate, I think the idea is a good one.<br /> <br /> Love the gourd idea too btw\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 10-03-2020, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T15:05:03-07:00","id":1416646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416091#post1416091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll talk it over with the players next session.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019ve annoyingly thought a little more about this potential charm suggestion and, yeaaah, it\u2019s spoilered below if of interest ahead of any discussion with the players. Now I\u2019ve vented this from my brain I\u2019ll stop going on about it. Promise.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Pre-reqs \u2013 on reflection I\u2019m not sure about Animal Empathy Technique, although I personally like Wild-Wandering Forester\u2019s Charm for it as it can introduce the fact that a suitable phenomenon is nearby. Maybe have it as just that, or more likely go with just, say, Mother-Of-Beasts Mastery as I know Melody has it (she\u2019d still have to get Occult 3 and an Occult specialty and buy three charms to get the full benefit, which is already possibly too much faff for the player to bother with).<br /> <br /> In an attempt to streamline the write-up and salvage something, I\u2019ve made it two charms, dropped it to just one trained elemental and made it E3. I initially shied away from one elemental as I figured that was encroaching into totem/spirit shape turf, but, after some thought, this seems <i>slightly</i> less cumbersome. I\u2019d greedily like to offer more options in terms of animals (or maybe instead a single more powerful option chosen at charm purchase) but that would make it significantly better than DEH so left it.<br /> <br /> So that all leads me to the below re-draft. Still not sure it works or is balanced, but hope it is of some interest/food for thought.<br /> <br /> <b>Wilderness-Progeny Dragon Prana</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m, 1a, 1wp; <b>Mins: </b>Survival 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>(Essence + Wits) days<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Mother-Of-Beasts Mastery<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood draws upon the potent forces that course through Creation's wilderness, weaving raw essence into the form of a bestial elemental servant to act as a companion, mount or guide.<br /> <br /> This charm functions in identical fashion to Dragon's Egg Hatched (Heirs of the Shogunate, pp. XX), with the exception that the base traits of the created elemental are either those of a wolf, horse or raiton (Exalted, pp. 562, 567, 570).<br /> <br /> <b>Dragon-Elemental Union Meditation</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2013; <b>Mins: </b>Survival 5, Occult 3, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Wilderness-Progeny Dragon Prana, Elemental Bond Meditation<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood partitions a portion of their own soul and infuses it into their chosen elemental servant, magnifying their bond and allowing them \u2013 with practise \u2013 to fashion their creation into increasingly potent forms.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood can now train one elemental created by Wilderness-Progeny Dragon Prana. This elemental must always be of the same base type and element and carry over its personality, memories and Intimacies whenever it is created, although its charm-granted mutations can vary to reflect the specific elemental manifestation it has been created from each time.<br /> <br /> Training functions as described in Exalted, pp. 554 with the additional caveats that the training roll is difficulty 3 and requires a specialty in Occult (Elementals) (however no Survival specialties are needed), no bonus dice are granted for intimacies and the elemental must be created in order to receive training \u2013 any successes carry over each time the elemental is created (albeit fading at the usual rate if the elemental is not trained again within three days). Charms can be used to enhance training as normal. The elemental can be trained in the latent or magical special attacks or merits of its base type (wolf, horse or raiton).<br /> <br /> The cost to create the trained elemental is increased to 5m, 1a, 1 wp, while the distance such an elemental can travel from the Dragon-Blood is increased to (Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence x 10). Should their trained elemental be destroyed the Dragon-Blood suffers one automatic health level of bashing damage and cannot create the elemental in question again for one week.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blood can undergo a cleansing ritual \u2013 perhaps a day\u2019s meditation in the presence of a suitable expression of the relevant element, such as a waterfall or mountain range \u2013 to purge the elemental from their soul. After this ritual the Dragon-Blood relinquishes the knowledge of how to create the trained elemental and can begin again with a new one. Any experience invested in the training of the original elemental is refunded. For example, a Dragon-Blood begins to train a \u2018wood wolf\u2019 elemental she has created. She cannot train any other type of created elemental unless she undertakes a cleansing ritual, at which point all experience points invested in training this elemental are refunded. After the ritual she can no longer create the trained wood wolf elemental but she can begin to train another elemental of any base type and element.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":"Essence x 10). Need to grow up. 10-04-2020, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T16:28:00-07:00","id":1416655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416645#post1416645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really like the idea behind Encompassing Flame Enhancement but agree with John it\u2019s waaaay too potent for its cost. Also, few quibbles on things as written, e.g. the heavy weapon stats thing, as a player/ST I\u2019d take that to mean ALL stats are swapped \u2013 so medium weapons lose their parry bonus, light weapons lose their accuracy etc, which doesn\u2019t seem the intention, and do already piercing weapons not gain any benefit?<br /> <br /> I\u2019d potentially instead look to do something like giving a group super-charged benefits of the Fire-aspected Dragon-Graced Weapon (say +3 Overwhelming or something) plus the environmental bonus as an alternative, costing the DB anima. But, to reiterate, I think the idea is a good one.<br /> <br /> Love the gourd idea too btw\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Damnable 3e.... *grumble grumble*<br /> <br /> Encompassing Flame Enhancement<br /> Cost: 8m, 1wp<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Melee 4, Essence 3<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are the flame, and Darkness, fears them. With a gesture, the Dragonblooded and his compatriot's weapon explodes into flame or glows red. The number of people who can benefit from this charm range from Essence X 3, and must be within Long Range. Bashing damage turns into lethal as blunt clubs turn red-hot, and lethal weaponry gains the piercing tags, and all weapons gaining a +5L damage. All weapons also gain either a +3 overwhelming or create a one-time environmental hazard of a bonfire upon striking an enemy, setting them alight, at the cost of a single willpower. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https: