he Dragon-Blood suffers one automatic health level of bashing damage and cannot create the elemental in question again for one week.<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blood can undergo a cleansing ritual \u2013 perhaps a day\u2019s meditation in the presence of a suitable expression of the relevant element, such as a waterfall or mountain range \u2013 to purge the elemental from their soul. After this ritual the Dragon-Blood relinquishes the knowledge of how to create the trained elemental and can begin again with a new one. Any experience invested in the training of the original elemental is refunded. For example, a Dragon-Blood begins to train a \u2018wood wolf\u2019 elemental she has created. She cannot train any other type of created elemental unless she undertakes a cleansing ritual, at which point all experience points invested in training this elemental are refunded. After the ritual she can no longer create the trained \u2018wood wolf\u2019 elemental but she can begin to train another elemental of any base type and element.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That is very, very cool.<br /> <br /> <i>Slightest</i> of downsides is that we played three hours before you posted that.<br /> <br /> I'll discuss a retcon next week (because this is a really cool idea), but we agreed a Phantom Steed reskin was cleaner yesterday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T01:17:01-07:00","id":1416697,"title":"","content":"Damned 3e. I love the evocation idea, but the entirely new combat system means that trying to create attack charms means trying to figure out how the entire new thing works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T07:15:18-07:00","id":1416722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416697#post1416697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damned 3e. I love the evocation idea, but the entirely new combat system means that trying to create attack charms means trying to figure out how the entire new thing works.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, this was something you had to do in 2e, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T13:15:31-07:00","id":1416752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416722#post1416722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, this was something you had to do in 2e, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But I didn't have to keep track of withering, decisive, and imitative.<br /> <br /> I got an idea for the gourd. Is it OK if I don't make any offensive charms and just write about environmental hazards?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:44:51-07:00","id":1416775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416752#post1416752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True. But I didn't have to keep track of withering, decisive, and imitative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that having to track Speed across Ticks in 2e was <i>at least as fiddly</i> as tracking withering damage across Initiative in 3e; it also meant that PCs with low-Speed weapons would get to take turns more often than the higher-Speed members of their circle, and that's <i>before</i> you factor in Rate.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I got an idea for the gourd. Is it OK if I don't make any offensive charms and just write about environmental hazards? </div> </div> </div>It's your artifact, if you don't think it should have attack stuff, that's fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-04-2020, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T15:46:43-07:00","id":1416777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1416775#post1416775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that having to track Speed across Ticks in 2e was <i>at least as fiddly</i> as tracking withering damage across Initiative in 3e.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's your artifact, if you don't think it should have attack stuff, that's fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an artifact based on the gourds of infinite wine you see in fiction from time to time. Only that 'wine' is their starting point, and it can eventually upgrade to be able to spit out storms and pyroclastic flow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T02:51:51-07:00","id":1416961,"title":"","content":"A spear according to Japanese Folklore. At first pretty normal looking, with some pretty good stats. Then you eventually gain evocations. First evocations lets you unleash an AoE effect upon anything you strike, basically releasing an explosion of energy. Higher evocations let you manipulate the environment around you, raising great walls of rock or turning entire sections of the area into swirling whirlpools of quicksand. And at the highest levels, you gain the power equivalent to wyld-shaping. By stabbing your spear into the ground and rotating it, you can transform the area around you in miles into the border marches middle marches, or the wyld, and do the reverse, turning sea into earth. <br /> <br /> <b>SWLIHN planning charm: </b><br /> <i>Essence 3, Bureaucracy 4</i><br /> <br /> A charm that encompasses all forms of pattern, cooperation, and hierarchy. The Infernal takes notice of all possible variables, putting them into practice, and then putting in the optimal path to victory, using her own understanding and logic. This supplements any wide-scale activity involving great masses of people, whether its the creating of a manse, evacuating an entire city, setting up a boot camp, or drafting in new tax law. Following the Infernal's plans, the speed and efficacy of the activity becomes superlative. The time taken to complete it is reduced by an order of magnitude, work that should take years taking months, work taking months taking weeks, and work that takes weeks takes days instead to complete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T05:54:42-07:00","id":1417134,"title":"","content":"Written for a character of mine, a sorceress who tried to fake being a Dragonblooded:<br /> <br /> <b>HESIESH\u2019S GIFT OF DIVINITY<br /> Cost</b>: 15sm, 1 wp<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Scene<br /> <br /> The sorcerer calls upon the great Immaculate Dragon of fire to cloak herself with raging flames, granting an assortment of benefits:<ul><li>She gains immunity to mundane heat hazards</li> <li>She may add her Essence to her soak and hardness against fire attacks.</li> <li>Her unarmed strikes gain the lethal and flame tags, and deal additional damage equal to her Essence.</li> <li>She may add her Essence to the damage she inflicts with mundane and magical fire attacks. This bonus is already included in the fire damage from Hesiesh\u2019s Gift.</li> <li>When a character begins their turn in short range of the sorcerer, they take [1/2 Essence, rounded up] points of initiative damage from the erupting flames. If they are in initiative crash, they instead take 1 level of lethal damage.</li> </ul><br /> A sorcerer who knows Hesiesh\u2019s Gift as her control spell adds two non-charm dice to their rolls against mundane heat hazards even when the spell is not active. When it is, she may choose whether or not characters in short range are affected by the aura.<br /> <br /> <i>Distortion (Goal Number: 15):</i> Distorting Hesieh\u2019s Gift of Divinity causes the sorcerer to be consumed by flames. A bondfire hazard appears at their current position, affecting all targets within short range.<br /> <br /> <br /> And for a player who wanted to lean into the dance-fighting idea of Battle Dancer Method a bit more:<br /> <br /> <b>DANCE OF FLASHING BLADES</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 5m, 1wp; Mins: Performance 5, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Simple<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Uniform<br /> <b>Duration</b>: One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Battle-Dancer Method<br /> <br /> The Solar makes a ballroom of the battlefield, incorporating the rhythm of steel-against-steel into her dance. As long as she remains on her feet and dancing, she may use her Performance in place of Dodge when calculating Evasion and when taking any combat action. If she makes a withering or decisive attack that overcomes her target\u2019s Resolve as well as their Evasion or Parry, they suffer a one success penalty when resisting her social influence for the duration of the scene.<br /> <br /> Performing a Dance of Flashing Blades counts as dancing for the purposes any charms which require the Solar to be dancing, such as Battle Dancer Method or Shining Expression Style. If she is knocked prone at any point while dancing, the effects of this charm end.<br /> <br /> <b>UNBROKEN MARTIAL PERFORMANCE</b><br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2m; Mins: Performance 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type</b>: Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: None<br /> <b>Duration</b>: Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms</b>: Respect-Commanding Attitude <br /> <br /> The Solar is grace and motion incarnate, her every movement a symphony for the eyes. When flurrying a Performance-based social influence action with another action, she may activate this charm to negate the usual flurry penalties.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T06:02:52-07:00","id":1417135,"title":"","content":"Well shit, I never thought of that. A spell that grants a multitude of benefits. I really need to make some stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T07:04:49-07:00","id":1417138,"title":"","content":"<b>DEADLY BALLET SWORD SWING</b><br /> Essence 2, Performance 3<br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Duration: instant <br /> Keywords: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are consummate performers, and where the elements dwell, there can be threatre. Even in the field of battle. The battle counts as one scene of using performance to build an intimacy using performance dice pool. This can be things like 'Bright Flowing Snowflake is the most beautiful and graceful woman of all' to 'Flaming Stone is a pathetic scoundrel'. Each fight counts as a scene of building a new intimacy. A single duel can instill a crowd with contempt towards the Realm. Multiple duels over the course of days can lead to revolts and rebellion. <br /> <br /> [spaceholder for effect if the DB wins]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-08-2020, 12:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T23:51:48-07:00","id":1417271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1417138#post1417138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>DEADLY BALLET SWORD SWING</b><br /> Essence 2, Performance 3<br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Duration: 1 scene<br /> Keywords: Reflexive<br /> <br /> The Dragonblooded are consummate performers, and where the elements dwell, there can be threatre. Even in the field of battle. This must be activated before combat. After this, the battle counts as one scene of using performance to convince onlookers of a single minor intimacy. This can be things like 'Bright Flowing Snowflake is the most beautiful and graceful woman of all' to 'Flaming Stone is a pathetic, cowardly scoundrel'. However, the intimacy must have something to do with the situation at hand and the performers. A brawl in a bar in the West will let the dragonblooded create intimacies of fear, respect or awe towards him, but will not let him instill intimacies of 'despise the realm'. Conversely, a duel in public with a Dragonblooded of the Realm will let him instill contempt in all citizenry who witness the duel.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay... but why?<br /> <br /> I'd rather take one measly action, or flurry, to take an Instill action than be 4m down for an entire fight. Heck, why can't I win the bar brawl, then use Performance to Instill an Intimacy of Fear on the observers by growling at them? Or win the duel then give a speech on the evils of empire?<br /> <br /> This Charm is &quot;pay 4m COMMITTED to avoid the Flurry penalty for circumstances where you don't have to Flurry anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd drop the restriction on it only being to Instill a new Minor Intimacy (to let each fight count as new evidence towards stronger Intimacies), and have it effect your foes (win or lose) as well as bystanders. Either drop the logical connection (so your bar Brawl can inspire people to topple the Realm) or have it Instill the Intimacy automatically without a roll. You could probably stand to also let applicable Performance Specialties (i.e. &quot;Acting&quot;) apply to combat rolls whilst the Charm is in effect, so the committed motes do something for you.<br /> <br /> It's a really good idea for a Charm. It's clearly based in enhancing the mundane with supranatural powers. Good thematics. Just needs a little more punch to be worth the XP/motes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T00:12:26-07:00","id":1417275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1417271#post1417271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay... but why?<br /> <br /> I'd rather take one measly action, or flurry, to take an Instill action than be 4m down for an entire fight. Heck, why can't I win the bar brawl, then use Performance to Instill an Intimacy of Fear on the observers by growling at them? Or win the duel then give a speech on the evils of empire?<br /> <br /> This Charm is &quot;pay 4m COMMITTED to avoid the Flurry penalty for circumstances where you don't have to Flurry anyway&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd drop the restriction on it only being to Instill a new Minor Intimacy (to let each fight count as new evidence towards stronger Intimacies), and have it effect your foes (win or lose) as well as bystanders. Either drop the logical connection (so your bar Brawl can inspire people to topple the Realm) or have it Instill the Intimacy automatically without a roll. You could probably stand to also let applicable Performance Specialties (i.e. &quot;Acting&quot;) apply to combat rolls whilst the Charm is in effect, so the committed motes do something for you.<br /> <br /> It's a really good idea for a Charm. It's clearly based in enhancing the mundane with supranatural powers. Good thematics. Just needs a little more punch to be worth the XP/motes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Argh shit. I wrote it wrongly. Each scene of fighting counts as a scene of building an intimacy, just that you have to start from minor. <br /> <br /> And I sorta meant that you 'spend 4 motes to activate this charm'. Spend. Not commit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T09:10:00-07:00","id":1417329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1417275#post1417275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Argh shit. I wrote it wrongly. Each scene of fighting counts as a scene of building an intimacy, just that you have to start from minor. <br /> <br /> And I sorta meant that you 'spend 4 motes to activate this charm'. Spend. Not commit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Motes are committed for the duration of the Charm. So duration should be Instant not One Scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-09T05:12:46-07:00","id":1417431,"title":"","content":"<b>Mack's Warming Mead</b><br /> Any kind of alcohol with the right thaumaturgical blessing. Mack's Warming Mead gives drinker a +2 bonus to resist frigate climates and adds a +1 to their stamina. A favourite staple amongst men of the north who have to work during winter, either due to emergencies or duty. The mead lasts for 24 hours per drink, and can be stretched for far longer if the drinker only takes periodic sips. In olden times when there were far more complex societies and there could be far more thaumaturges, these were produced in batches for all to enjoy. Now they are only for the needy and the elite. <br /> <br /> Sidenote: Goddamn I hate the way they put the alchemy rituals in Oadenol's codex<br /> <br /> Name (Minimum Degree, Attribute, Dif\ufb01culty, Casting Time)<br /> <br /> Fire Draught (Intelligence attribute, Difficulty 3, Casting time of 1 hour, costs 1wp)<br /> <br /> An alchemy ritual known and quite popular with the Shamans of the North. Fire Draught is a 1 hour long ritual which a shaman mixes several specialized herbs (Resource 2) with pestle and mortar, and then boils it in a cauldron, before taking the residue and mixing it with alcohol. Matching the difficulty lets you produce enough residue for 20 bottles of mead (24 hours of the 2 dice bonus), with each extra success letting you produce an extra 20. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-18T18:51:01-07:00","id":1418922,"title":"","content":"Terrestrial spell:<br /> <br /> Cozy Homely Home<br /> <br /> Keywords: Ritual<br /> <br /> Some would look askance at the strange things sorcerers create. Things like demonic and elemantal creations, ghosts of the dead, strange alterations to the landscape, and trees which resemble thrones and stone which have run like water and solidified. Others are more to the point, asking: &quot;Why is there a house in the middle of the woods?&quot;<br /> <br /> This spell summons a small house, far smaller than that of orchid pavilion, the equivalent of a 2 or 3 story house, able to hold up to at most 50 people. The house itself protects against up to -4 environmental penalties, letting the people within hide from harsh weather, but nothing absurd like lava. Supplies within it are infinite, with infinite water, lighting, heat, food, and etc. Within the building the inhabitants count as at rest or in deep meditation for purposes of mote recovery and recovery from exhaustion. The house has the same stats as a fortress manse composed out of reinforced metal (check Sandact6's notes) and automatically has wards to protect against spiritual and enemy incursion. All attempts to break into the house contain a -3 penalty, unless they are invited inside by an inhabitant.<br /> <br /> Blessing of swift desert sands<br /> <br /> Bureaucracy 4, essence 2, Cecylene.<br /> Cost: 8m<br /> <br /> An alteration of speed the wheels. The leaders of a particular endeavour come together in a single ceremony before embarking in a single large scale project endeavour . This does not need to come from the entire organisation. An attempt to reform the entire government will require all ministers and the president to come together. An attempt to say, build gigantic Road network through the dense countryside will require the minister of transport and his immediate subordinates, several labour union heads, and cartographers. The ceremony can take forms from a formal dinner, hours of chanting and prayer, or a wild rave. At the end of the scene the leader of the social unit (its highest status member) pays a single temporary Willpower, letting the Infernal reflexively work her magic on the organisation. This reduces time spent on the project using the same calculations for speed the wheels.<br /> <br /> A sacrifice can be made to enhance the proceedings, Cecylene taking the tribute and granting even greater power. The bonus is the resources value divided by 2, rounded up, and can be added to the Infernals essence for calculations or as a bonus to all rolls carrying out the project. A resources 4 sacrifice can add 2 to the Infernals essence for the calculation of the time decrease, or add 2 dice to any roll made to further the project.<br /> <br /> edit: <br /> <br /> Example: <br /> <br /> Burning Waters has recently outlawed slavery, and wish to prosecute cruel slave masters, compensate slaves, reunite slavery, and re-order the economy to wean it off the dependence on slaves. However such an action will take years, even decades. Thus he makes a Resource 5 sacrifice to one of his Infernal allies, The Woman of the Wastes, an Essence 3 Infernal. The time needed to carry out the action drops from decades, to years, to seasons, to months, to weeks, to days. Miraculously the entire effort takes less than a week to finish, and the entire economy is booming along. Not satisfied with this and realizing the uncertainty of the new changes, he organises a feast and festival in the capital city with a sacrifices of Resources 4. His staff, normally good with 6 to 7 dice, now have 9 dice to prepare the festivities, and the festival is a smashing success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 10-19-2020, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T09:00:23-07:00","id":1419013,"title":"","content":"Is Secure Shelter meant to be permenant?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T10:55:04-07:00","id":1419043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1419013#post1419013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Secure Shelter meant to be permenant?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Just a week or so. <br /> <br /> .... I think I made it too inflexible. I should give it a bunch of different possible stats, and then you can roll and distribute successes as dots, like the book of the Emerald circle's version of Invocation of the Living Ship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value"