s=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T06:31:25-07:00","id":1420452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1420447#post1420447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas for other evocations then?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the siege weapon?<br /> <br /> Your attacks get bonuses on battle groups and fortresses, and can split up into multiple bolts. <br /> <br /> Can force enemies to flee if you hit them with a sustained bombardment.<br /> <br /> Enemies formation get disrupted by a hit, making them easy pickings for other battle groups. Put this as a temporary penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T06:59:09-07:00","id":1420459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1420447#post1420447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ideas for other evocations then?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, which one are you going with? Lightning ballista, or implosion bow? I'd argue that the Evocations one should be able to develop should be different from the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-27T07:32:03-07:00","id":1420472,"title":"","content":"Lets say the implosion bow..<br /> <br /> oh<br /> <br /> Just thought Glorious Solar Bow Glorious Solar Saber Glorious Solar Plate all say repurchases will let you buy them evocations<br /> <br /> Ideas for those evocations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-27-2020, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T00:38:45-07:00","id":1420627,"title":"","content":"They both say to use the Solar\u2019s personality and iconic anima manifestation as inspiration, but nonetheless the only way I\u2019ve ever thought of to square the circle of what Evocations are supported by a composition of pure solidified Solar Essence and a \u201clegend\u201d of being a Solar Charm is to just cheat it by saying \u201cAny hypothetical Solar Charm whose description hinges on having a Glorious Solar Saber/Plate is an Evocation of Glorious Solar Saber/Plate.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-28T09:51:42-07:00","id":1420698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1420472#post1420472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lets say the implosion bow..<br /> <br /> oh<br /> <br /> Just thought Glorious Solar Bow Glorious Solar Saber Glorious Solar Plate all say repurchases will let you buy them evocations<br /> <br /> Ideas for those evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>These should be based on the Solars personality and deeds\u2014they are the Solars Essence made a weapon or armor. A blood thirsty Zentig might have a blade that drives others into a frenzy, a wise Dawn might have armor that predicts enemy attacks, etc","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-29T20:56:28-07:00","id":1420926,"title":"","content":"Oh whats a good cost for Giving Extra initiative? on an evocation<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh ideas for charms?<br /> <br /> Add ons to food gathering Method and Ration enhancing practice<br /> <br /> <br /> Letting y ou find not so meager fare.<br /> <br /> Like hunt down rare animals or find tasty hard to find herbs you can use to cook with (or sell for a profit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 10-30-2020, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T11:51:36-07:00","id":1421189,"title":"","content":"Hey guys. I got an idea for charms.<br /> <br /> But first, a question. Cecylene locust mana plague. What so you think of its mind affecting function? Good? Bad? Should be toggable? Shouldn't exist? Should be a bit more subtle?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 11-01-2020, 01:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T12:48:56-07:00","id":1421195,"title":"","content":"Locust <b>Mana </b>Plague<br /> <br /> <br /> how would you make it more subtle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T13:45:24-07:00","id":1421205,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1421189#post1421189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey guys. I got an idea for charms.<br /> <br /> But first, a question. Cecylene locust man's plague. What so you think of its mind affecting function? Good? Bad? Should be toggable? Shouldn't exist? Should be a bit more subtle?</div> </div> </div> </div>For my 3E game we treated it as a straight &quot;Automatically succeed at an Instill action for the Principle &quot;I obey the laws of hell&quot; regardless of Resolve&quot;. Like any other Minor Intimacy, it can be resisted for 1WP, and only raised to Major with a Supporting Intimacy. Otherwise, brightly colored locusts feeds you for a day if you eat one, can be candied to preserve them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-31T15:18:23-07:00","id":1421220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1420926#post1420926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh whats a good cost for Giving Extra initiative? on an evocation</div> </div> </div> </div>I use the rule of thumb that 1 initiative is worth between 1 and 2 motes.<br /> This can depend on things like what splat it's for (or for evocations whether it's resonant/neutral/dissonant), how high the requirements and prerequisites are, how often the charm can be used, how reliably it gives the initiative, etc.<br /> <br /> For some examples - Reed in the Wind spends 2i in place of 2m, Flow Like Blood upgrades it to 1i in place of 2m.<br /> Fire and Stones Strike spends 1m for 1 withering or decisive damage. 1 decisive damage is like 1i if you hit, so like (probability of hitting) initiative in general. 1 withering damage gains you on average 1/2 an initiative, and costs the enemy the same amount, so is also worth in total (probability of hitting) initiative<br /> Striving Aftershock Method spends 2m for 2i, but only after landing a decisive attack","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23597-autxauty","name":"autXautY","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T01:47:58-07:00","id":1421271,"title":"","content":"<b>MOTHERS FEED THEIR CHILDREN</b><br /> Mins: Essence 1<br /> Keyword: Water, stackable<br /> <br /> The Infernal blesses a large lake sized body of water with the Kimberryian Essence. Or more accurately, the Kimberryian essence that tends to nurture her children. This causes the beings within the body of water to quicken and grow at supernatural speeds, and all harvests of the food within are nutritious, tasty, and bring in rich hauls. The food can take the form of seaweed, underwater insects, crustaceans, fish, jellyfish, or marine mammals. A single usage of this charm lasts for a year and a day, and feeds a Essence + 1 size population. This can be stacked up to three times on the same body of water.<br /> <br /> Eating this food is nutritious and prevents all form of malnutrition. All mealtimes involving this food counts as a scene of building a minor intimacy of &quot;gratitude and thankfulness&quot; to the person who used the charm. Coincidentally the charm kills all parasites and diseases like cholera and tapeworm, burning them with caustic acid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-01T15:27:37-08:00","id":1421347,"title":"","content":"Some ideas for an evocation for a woodd aspected Immaculates Powerbow think its reasonable to let it be used as a wrackstaff if hes in a Melee?<br /> <br /> Want to grant some benefits to Melees and to ranged combat too.<br /> <br /> Wood Immaculates will probaly study archery charms too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","user":"Prince of the Night","date":". 11-03-2020, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T10:57:54-08:00","id":1421652,"title":"","content":"SWLIHN Charms! <br /> <br /> <b>ORGANISATION SYNCHRONIZATION</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 2m<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Essence: 2<br /> Prereq: SWLIHN excellency<br /> <br /> SWLIHN is the patron and goddess of all systems, all hierarchies, and all patterns. In crystal facets, in fractals, and in the patterns that humans organise themselves into. The Infernal blesses an organisation with the efficiency and simplicity of She Who Lives in Her Name. It can be a girl scout troop, a restaurant chain, a manufacturing company, a bank, or an orphanage. Either way, things are done with near perfect precision and a minimum of fuss. Aberrations, like corruption or inefficiency or redundant paperwork, are burned away, made to shape up, or thrown out. This removes corrupt or indolent members, or wasteful practices. All members gain a minor positive intimacy to the organization and the organization's goals, whether its checking licenses or setting up death camps. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>PATTERN PROTECTION PRANA</b><br /> <br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Essence: 1<br /> Prerequisites: Organisation synchronization<br /> <br /> SWLIHN is crystalline perfection, and her facets are often the last thing Chaos ever sees before they are transmuted to Order. Same goes for anything that attempts to damage the blessed patterns and organisations of SWLIHN. Everyone in the organization with an intimacy that can be interpreted to advance the organization's goals uses the intimacy in their resolve against any bribe, intimidate, threaten, or social attacks, as well as gaining the Infernal's essence in bonus dice. A clerk trying to write up someone for pretending to be a thaumaturge can be convinced to wait for a week for a witness or paperwork. A noblewoman trying to seduce an investigator or magistrate to ignore the allegations of Necromancy will find her efforts stymied.<br /> <br /> This is upgraded at Essence 3 to extend to physical issues, like rolls to resist hardship when working in a hot desert or fighting off attackers trying to sabotage a project. Or even resisting diseases that prevent you from working. <br /> <br /> This effect ceases if the individual leaves the organization. <br /> <br /> <b>COG-ENHANCING-CORRECTION*</b><br /> Cost: 4m<br /> Essence: 2<br /> Prerequisites: Organisation Synchronization<br /> Duration: Task<br /> <br /> Sometimes you just have to work with the materials you have. No matter. They can be improved and enhanced. All people involved in a project are considered to have (Essence x 2) bonus to carry it out and removes the untrained penalty. An Infernal with Essence 2 who uses this charm is considered to have workers who have 4 extra dice to carry out any roll, whether in crafting, bureaucracy, or research. Workers are considered to have a major intimacy to completing the project. <br /> <br /> <b>MASS COORDINATION CHANT</b><br /> <br /> Essence: 3<br /> Prerequisites: Cog-Enhancing-Correction<br /> Duration: Task<br /> <br /> <br /> An upgrade to Cog-Enhancing-Corection. As long as there are great masses of disparate elements, SWLIHN can take them, organize them, and bring them to new heights that would be considered impossible by other more limited and chaotic minds. This charm enhances any wide-scale project enhanced by cog-enhancing-correction, increasing its possible scope by (Essence). A great palace which should have been built in years now instead takes mere months. Materials spontaneously transform into better vesions of themselves, or craftsmen find out new techniques that let them do more with less. Difficulty of extended rolls, time between extended rolls, and resources costs are considered to be reduced by (Essence). <br /> <br /> Cecylene Society Charms: <br /> <br /> All is Sand<br /> Mins: Essence 3<br /> Prerequisites: Locust Mana Plague<br /> <br /> All things turn to sand and grit. All things owe themselves to hierarchy. All things are touched by the infinite desert. All actions to the infernal which can be constituted as 'prayer', count as a scene of building an intimacy to the infernal. This can include reciting a pledge of allegiance to the Infernal, reading out loud poetry praising her and her goodness in class, or reciting a promise in her name. This can build up to major intimacy of loyalty and devotion, but no more than that. <br /> <br /> YOU OWE ME<br /> Cost: 3m<br /> Mins: Essence 2<br /> Prerequisites: Verdant emptiness Endowment.<br /> <br /> Even if she did not benefit them directly, Cecylene's sands still touch people when they benefit from her actions. This lets the Infernal use her actions as leverage towards people who do not have direct contact with her. If the Infernal helps direct a trading caravan to a town, leading to booming business or new popular goods on the market, then her target counts as having a minor intimacy of gratefulness to her. If the Infernal helps with something even more, like creating Water for a community who's well had dried up or shattering killing the slavers who had kidnapped a towns people, she can have the target have a major intimacy of gratefulness to her.*** <br /> <br /> *This needs a lot of rebalancing to make sure it isn't broken. <br /> <br /> ** I really need help in writing up organizational charms. <br /> <br /> *** This is not very well done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T12:04:59-08:00","id":1421659,"title":"","content":"<b>Regalia of the Raiton (Moonsilver silken armor, Artifact 4)</b><br /> <br /> The dark feathers of spirit raitons have been joined together to dark gray and black enchanted silk via a fine mesh of moonsilver wire. Gloves and boots and belt are likewise threaded through with the shimmering magical metal. The last piece of this terrifying regalia is a menacing bird-faced mask, the creation of Shalrina, Daimyo of Faces.<br /> The Regalia of the Raiton does not count as armor for the purpose of compatibility with martial arts.<br /> <br /> <b>Attunement:</b> 4m<br /> <b>Type:</b> Light (Soak +5, Hardness +4, Mobility Penalty -0)<br /> <b>Tags:</b> Silent, Special<br /> <b>Hearthstone slots:</b> 2<br /> <b>Era:</b> Reign of the Shadow Deliberative<br /> <br /> <b>Evocations of the Regalia</b>\u200b<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>On Wings of Night</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 1m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 1<br /> <i>Type:</i> Reflexive<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> Resonant<br /> <i>Duration:</i> One scene<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> None<br /> Drawing on ancient memories of the hunt, the Exalt spreads wide her cloak and glides; this uses the rules for the Essence glider on Exalted p. 603.<br /> <i>Resonant:</i> An user who is Resonant with the Regalia may pay 4m while gliding to supplement a Rush against a ground-based opponent; if successful, she may apply the extra successes as dice on the damage roll of her next withering attack against the Rushed opponent.<br /> <br /> <b>Swift Sable Thought</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 3m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 2<br /> <i>Type:</i> Simple<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> One scene<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> On Wings of Night<br /> No puzzle is beyond the raiton's cunning; while this Evocation is active, the Exalt may reroll ones on rolls to Case Scene, Profile Character, Read Intentions, or diagnose a patient, and denies her ones to enemy magic. If the information she gathers with such rolls are pertinent to an Intelligence-based roll in the same scene, that roll gains a similar benefit.<br /> <br /> <b>Raiton Finds Corpse</b><br /> <i>Cost</i>: --; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 2<br /> <i>Type:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> On Wings of Night<br /> The eyes of the raiton are attuned to death, its tongue to the taste of carrion. The Exalt gains double 9s on Perception rolls that would reveal a corpse or other remains, or an undead foe in stealth. If the roll already benefits from double 9s, it instead gains a non-Charm success.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Messenger of the Dead</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 3m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 2<br /> <i>Type:</i> Reflexive<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> One scene<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> On Wings of Night, Spirit-Detecting Glance OR Perceiving the Hidden World OR Spirit-Detecting Mirror Technique<br /> The Exalt grants her voice to the bodiless; if she witnesses a dematerialized spirit with one of her Charms, she may act as a conduit to the material for it. Doing so lets the spirit speak with her voice, though it is apparent to onlookers that the words are not her own. The spirit uses its own dice pools for social influence.<br /> If the Exalt desires to speak for herself again or otherwise wishes to sever the connection, this Evocation may not be used on the same spirit in the same scene.<br /> <i>Special:</i> This Evocation is unlocked for free when the Exalt delivers a message to a material creature on the behalf of a dematerialized spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Pronouncement of the Feathered Justice</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 3m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 2<br /> <i>Type:</i> Supplemental<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> Resonant<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Instant<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> Swift Sable Thought, Black Messenger of the Dead<br /> The raiton spots the flaw in her foe's armor; realizing this, the foe is filled with terror of her thrusting beak. This Evocation supplements a Threaten action using information gleaned from a successful Read Intentions or Profile Character action against the target. The Threaten gains double 9s, and if successful, the target automatically gains a Tie of fear toward the Exalt at Minor intensity.<br /> The Tie cannot be eroded normally, but may be suppressed for a scene by spending 1wp. Once the target has spent (Essence) Willpower suppressing his fear the Intimacy may be removed normally.<br /> <i>Resonant:</i> This Evocation may be repurchased at Essence 4 creates the imposed Tie at Major intensity.<br /> <br /> <b>Night and Day Method</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> --(5m, +1 Limit); <i>Mins:</i> Essence 3<br /> <i>Type:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Swift Sable Thought, Raiton Finds Corpse, Heart-Eclipsing Shroud<br /> When the Solar assumes one of her personas via Heart-Eclipsing Shroud, the Raiton Regalia shifts its appearance to fit the persona's concept: for a wealthy noble, it might take the appearance of a black silk frock coat chased with silver feathers and a silver circlet; for a pirate captain, it may be a cloth-of-silver tricorne hat with a tattered black naval waistcoat and silver rings. Furthermore, the Solar may spend five motes and gain 1 Limit to assume the persona over the course of one round. However, the Solar may not use Night and Day Method to speed her next change of personas in this fashion.<br /> <i>Special:</i> This Evocation cannot be purchased with experience points; it is unlocked for free when the Solar spends at least one scene each in two different personas over the course of one story.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodcurdling Reafan Banner</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 5m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 3<br /> <i>Type:</i> Reflexive<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> One scene<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> Black Messenger of the Dead, Swift Sable Thought<br /> Phantasmal raitons trail in the Exalt's wake, speaking the words of the dead. The spectral raitons penalize Stealth attempts by the Exalt as though her anima was at Glowing (but does not stack with the penalty of a Glowing anima). She adds an automatic non-Charm success to her threaten actions; enemy battle groups raise the difficulty of rout and rally rolls by 1.<br /> The spirit-raitons may also serve as relays to an allied battle group, allowing the Solar to make Intelligence-based command actions out to extreme range at no penalty.<br /> <br /> <b>Black Feathered Shadow</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> --(3m); <i>Mins:</i> Essence 3<br /> <i>Type:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Raiton Finds Corpse, Black Messenger of the Dead<br /> Darkness embraces the raiton and hides it from its prey. The first time in a scene that the Exalt successfully Crashes or incapacitates a non-trivial enemy from stealth, she may spend 3m to reflexively make a Threaten roll against all enemies who witness the takedown, ignoring the penalty for influencing multiple targets. Her demands on the Threaten action must be actions relevant to the immediate combat.<br /> If any of the targets have been affected by Pronouncement of the Feathered Justice, witnessing the takedown increases the Tie of fear to the Exalt by one degree of intensity.<br /> <br /> <b>Many Graves Burial</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 6m, 1wp; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 3<br /> <i>Type:</i> Supplemental<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> Mute<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Instant<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> Raiton Finds Corpse, Swift Sable Thought<br /> A scavenger knows what a scavenger seeks; the Exalt supplements a Conceal Evidence action, allowing her to hide the truth in moments. Any 1s and 2s rolled on a Case Scene action cause the seeker to lose a success. If the seeker fails to find any clues, the Exalt regains a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Shining Silver Theft</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 4m; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 3<br /> <i>Type:</i> Supplemental<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> Mute, Psyche<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Instant<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> Raiton Finds Corpse, Black Messenger of the Dead<br /> Eyes shining with avarice, the Exalt plants an illusion, to ensure her clever theft will go unnoticed. This Evocation enhances a pickpocketing attempt; if her successful roll is also higher than her victim's Resolve, not only does she steal the item, but the victim believes he still carries the pilfered item, seeing an illusory copy in his mind's eye. The belief may be broken by spending 2wp, but if the discrepancy is pointed out to him or he attempts to use the stolen item and finds it doesn't work, the cost is decreased by 1wp.<br /> <br /> <b>Memories of the Rook</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 1wp; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 4<br /> <i>Type:</i> Reflexive<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Instant<br /> <i>Prerequisite Charms:</i> Swift Sable Thought, Black Feathered Shadow, Spirit-Maintaining Maneuver<br /> Even if the Solar has forgotten her purpose, the Regalia remembers. If a Psyche effect removes, overwrites, or erases her memories, she may restore her true memories by spending a Willpower after either successfully asserting Resolve in defense of an Intimacy tied to the lost memories, or by using the Intimacy in a decision point. If an enemy was responsible for the effect that caused the Solar to lose her memories, the sudden shattering of the enchantment causes him to lose a point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>Uncanny Feathered Intruder</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> --; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 4<br /> <i>Type:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> None<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Permanent<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Black Messenger of the Dead, Many Graves Burial<br /> The Exalt's persistence flies her through the most heavily-guarded fortress. Succeeding on an opposed Stealth roll against a non-trivial character grants her two motes. These motes can only be spent on Charms to create or enhance further Stealth attempts.<br /> <br /> <b>Grim Psychopomp Method</b><br /> <i>Cost:</i> 3m, 1wp; <i>Mins:</i> Essence 4<br /> <i>Type:</i> Simple<br /> <i>Keywords:</i> Resonant<br /> <i>Duration:</i> Indefinite<br /> <i>Prerequisites:</i> Raiton Finds Corpse, Pronouncement of the Feathered Justice<br /> Following in the raiton's path, a wraith's bonds are stricken and he flies free. The Exalt may, with a touch, subsume a willing ghost into her anima; the ghost takes the form of a spectral raiton. The Exalt may use the ghost's Major and Defining Intimacies to defend against social influence as though they were hers. For the rest of the scene after she does so, however, she must act in accordance with that Intimacy.<br /> If the Exalt encounters the being responsible for the death that created a ghost she has subsumed, she may use Pronouncement of the Feathered Justice on him as if she had pierced his Guile. Incapacitating the killer or otherwise ensuring that justice is served lets the ghost move on into Lethe.<br /> <br /> \u200b<i>\u200bResonant</i>\u200b: As the ghost fades away, it vents a point of the Exalt's Limit.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-03-2020, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T19:30:48-08:00","id":1423442,"title":"","content":"<b>GLORIOUS SOLAR BUILDING</b><br /> Costs: 15m, 1wp Mins: Craft 5, Essence 3<br /> Type: Simple<br /> Keyword: Obvious<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite: Thousand-Forge Hands<br /> <br /> Good craftsmen can make a sword in half the time. Very good craftsmen can make swords in mere hours. Supernatural craftsmen can create a sword out of haematite with a mere wring of their hands. Some craftsmen can make things from nothing.<br /> <br /> The solar completes a single mundane superior project in a single moment of pure excellence, the world obeying her command, reshaping itself. With materials at hand, this charm can be used once a week, and the materials leap into the air to spontaneously form the project. Without materials, the light from the anima flares to coalescing into a solid building, and can be used once a year. This can also be used to create large numbers of major projects, ranging from having a thousand swords burst out of the sand, or have dust coalesce around your soldier's clothes to form impervious armour.<br /> <br /> Stunts are recommended.<br /> <br /> <b>METAMORPHIC PRAYER</b><br /> <br /> Sorcerous working: Terrestrial 3/ Celestial 1<br /> <br /> &quot;I wish to transform, into a newer, better, me!&quot;<br /> <br /> This working was created at the behest of someone who was truly miserable with the conflict between the talents he had, the talents he wanted, and the duties he wanted. A single shrine with an alter, with a single unquenchable flame within. Toss a sacrifice within the flames. It will not harm you. Whether it is pot brownies, coins, gold, silver, or a small wooden horse carved by your son. Spend a willpower, and the sorcerous working will continue. This lets you convert abilities, attributes, and merits on a dot by dot basis. A wandering swordsman an become a social butterfly. A strongman wrestler can become a scholar. This can only be done willingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 11-14-2020, 03:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T19:49:17-08:00","id":1423447,"title":"","content":"\u201cSuperior project\u201d would not be \u201ca sword,\u201d it would be \u201ca daiklave,\u201d or \u201ca palace.\u201d<br /> <br /> Not especially big on the idea of instantly building either of those out of literally nothing but the light of your anima (because then what\u2019s the point of Glorious Solar Saber)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T19:51:53-08:00","id":1423448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423447#post1423447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cSuperior project\u201d would not be \u201ca sword,\u201d it would be \u201ca daiklave,\u201d or \u201ca palace.\u201d<br /> <br /> Not especially big on the idea of instantly building either of those out of literally nothing but the light of your anima (because then what\u2019s the point of Glorious Solar Saber)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Reread the charm. <br /> <br /> I'm not going to say any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T21:27:15-08:00","id":1423464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423448#post1423448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Reread the charm.<br /> <br /> I'm not going to say any more.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If someone asks either ignore them or answer them, don't assume you've been clear.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T21:46:29-08:00","id":1423467,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This can also be used to create large numbers of major projects </div> </div> </div>A superior project can encompass many, many major projects at once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T22:05:33-08:00","id":1423468,"title":"","content":"The use of it to make a sword versus many swords isn\u2019t the bone of my contention - I don\u2019t think being able to make a daiklave or palace in an eyeblink, all without having to <i>get</i> anything to do so, is good for telling a story. <br /> <br /> Part of the reason 3E artifacts are interesting is because you\u2019ve got to go acquire the frozen blood of a behemoth or forge mathematical impossibilities out of the Wyld and work them into the blade; these are both intended to tell a cool story, <i>and</i> to inform the nature of the Evocations the finished artifact will have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-12T22:36:05-08:00","id":1423474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423468#post1423468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The use of it to make a sword versus many swords isn\u2019t the bone of my contention - I don\u2019t think being able to make a daiklave or palace in an eyeblink, all without having to <i>get</i> anything to do so, is good for telling a story.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason 3E artifacts are interesting is because you\u2019ve got to go acquire the frozen blood of a behemoth or forge mathematical impossibilities out of the Wyld and work them into the blade; these are both intended to tell a cool story, <i>and</i> to inform the nature of the Evocations the finished artifact will have.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have just edited it. <br /> <br /> So, better now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T03:06:48-08:00","id":1423503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423474#post1423474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, better now?</div> </div> </div> </div>Better, but I still don\u2019t like it. <br /> <br /> Being able to build a maximum-security prison facility around your opponent <i>as he\u2019s attacking you</i> doesn\u2019t seem like it should be kosher.<br /> <br /> A character with this Charm would never want for Resources dots again, because he can just sneeze out a fifteen-foot-high statue of the Scarlet Empress giving the middle finger, all carved from a single diamond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T03:36:37-08:00","id":1423510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423503#post1423503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better, but I still don\u2019t like it.<br /> <br /> Being able to build a maximum-security prison facility around your opponent <i>as he\u2019s attacking you</i> doesn\u2019t seem like it should be kosher.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologise if I misunderstand you. <br /> <br /> But... what's the difference? Someone with CNNT can literally run into a soup kitchen, and run out 5 seconds later with a rapid-firing grenade launcher. Thousand Forge Hands lets you create an entire palace within mere weeks when it would normally take years or decades. This is a extension of that. Slightly overpowered, yes, but a major project is something like a house or a small apartment, with superior projects being something like a mansion or a dam project. With CNNT alone you *can* build an entire prison around your opponent. Just a smaller one. <br /> <br /> I mean, if its that bad I can just throw in a caveat that prevents it from being used in combat, not dissimilar to the ritual keyword for sorcery spells. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">A character with this Charm would never want for Resources dots again, because he can just sneeze out a fifteen-foot-high statue of the Scarlet Empress giving the middle finger, all carved from a single diamond.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>You're an Essence 3 Solar with Craft 5. Money is already something that you *can* get. I mean, what scenario are you thinking of by this time?<br /> <br /> You barely need infrastructure. You barely need the processed materials for most crafting. You can literally stroll into a forest and walk out with masterpieces that would be amongst the greatest in Creation. You can grab blocks of marble and kick them into the next Galatea. You can stroll up to a mortal king, and tell him that he can have a new palace, a new irrigation system, or a new manse. All things which are worth Resources 5 to any ruler, and you can get it on the cheap. Multiple ones at the same time. Your expertise, power, and gifts are literally near priceless, especially in a world where there are no vast construction machines. <br /> <br /> Yes, you'll never want for Resource dots again. <br /> <br /> But then again, that's a bit of a moot point, considering that with the bare minimal effort you can already get Resources 5 easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-13T05:24:09-08:00","id":1423527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423510#post1423510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... what's the difference?</div> </div> </div> </div>With regular crafting, you\u2019re making something out of something. If you want to build a palace, you\u2019ve got to haul stone to where you want the thing built, or pay to have it shipped in. If you want the Empress Middle Finger statue, you\u2019ll need to get the services of a powerful Earth elemental to secure a diamond that large. <br /> <br /> Your Charm literally lets them make it out of nothing, taking all the story potential of those previous scenes and burying it in six different garbage bags hidden around the city.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Someone with CNNT can literally run into a soup kitchen, and run out 5 seconds later with a rapid-firing grenade launcher. </div> </div> </div>Only in Exalted Modern.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thousand Forge Hands lets you create an entire palace within mere weeks when it would normally take years or decades. </div> </div> </div>But still <i>some</i> time, and out of <i>some</i> materials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a extension of that. Slightly overpowered, yes\u2026 </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not just overpowered - it\u2019s a game-changer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With CNNT alone you *can* build an entire prison around your opponent. Just a smaller one. </div> </div> </div>CNNT is Simple; the Charm you made is Reflexive, meaning you can use it <i>in response to an attack</i>.<br /> <br /> I can tell a story with something. I can\u2019t tell a story with nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 11-13-2020, 08:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T00:12:45-08:00","id":1423687,"title":"","content":"Oh didnt see it explicitly anywhere but can I voluntarily up the level of an artifact im buying to increase its potential evocations?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T00:38:42-08:00","id":1423691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423687#post1423687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh didnt see it explicitly anywhere but can I voluntarily up the level of an artifact im buying to increase its potential evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, doesn't seem to break any rules. I&quot;ll rule it as a superior/ major project to increase the artifacts, and throw in an exotic ingredient cost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T00:44:30-08:00","id":1423692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423527#post1423527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regular crafting, you\u2019re making something out of something. If you want to build a palace, you\u2019ve got to haul stone to where you want the thing built, or pay to have it shipped in. If you want the Empress Middle Finger statue, you\u2019ll need to get the services of a powerful Earth elemental to secure a diamond that large.<br /> <br /> Your Charm literally lets them make it out of nothing, taking all the story potential of those previous scenes and burying it in six different garbage bags hidden around the city.<br /> <br /> Only in Exalted Modern.<br /> <br /> But still <i>some</i> time, and out of <i>some</i> materials.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not just overpowered - it\u2019s a game-changer.<br /> <br /> CNNT is Simple; the Charm you made is Reflexive, meaning you can use it <i>in response to an attack</i>.<br /> <br /> I can tell a story with something. I can\u2019t tell a story with nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, by this time I've pretty much done with this charm. So yeah, thanks for the review, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T05:01:47-08:00","id":1423724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423687#post1423687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh didnt see it explicitly anywhere but can I voluntarily up the level of an artifact im buying to increase its potential evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd treat reforging an Artifact to a higher dot level as a Repair project. But, RAW, the answer is &quot;no&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-14T05:44:04-08:00","id":1423727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1423687#post1423687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh didnt see it explicitly anywhere but can I voluntarily up the level of an artifact im buying to increase its potential evocations?</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean, when making the character, can you declare that the artifact is of a higher dot rating than it was listed as in a book?<br /> <br /> If so, then yeah, there's nothing stopping you. But really you could just ignore the number limit on evocations, it's going to be fine if you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4578-zale","name":"Zale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4578_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T07:11:36-08:00","id":1425508,"title":"","content":"One of our players is after a homebrewed upgrade to Blade-Deflecting Palm that makes it elementally neutral (and potentially help him fight a Lunar that wrecked a previous Wyld Hunt he was on). This is my very rough first pass. Questions for the forum if anyone has the time:<br /> <br /> 1. A theoretical Essence 5 DB could use this to make an opponent re-roll up to 8 successes on an attack roll (albeit for 12m, 1i, 1a). That feels too powerful. Should I pare this back so it's either the effects of regular BDP or this, with the proviso you can't use both on the same attack? Or something else? Or walk away entirely?<br /> <br /> 2. Is its wording clear? I tend to find if it takes me a lot of words to explain a charm then its generally a bad charm in the first place, and I think this might fall foul of that. The idea is that re-rolls caused by 2s cost 2m.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <b>Elemental Deflection Stance</b><br /> <b>Cost:</b> \u2013 (2m per die, +1a); <b>Mins: </b>Brawl 4, Essence 2<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Blade-Deflecting Palm<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood\u2019s channels her anima into her defences, using its power to drive aside her opponents\u2019 most deadly attacks. When she attempts to block an attack from close range using Blade-Deflecting Palm, she can expend a level of her anima in order to make the charm apply to (Dragon-Blood\u2019s Essence/2, rounded up) 2s in her opponent\u2019s roll in addition to its normal effects, although the Dragon-Blood has to pay two motes for such re-rolls rather than the usual one. Such uses of Blade-Deflecting Palm are the same Aspect as the Dragon-Blood\u2019s native element.<br /> <br /> In her native Aura, a successful block involving this charm causes the Dragon-Blood\u2019s opponent to lose one Initiative, which the Dragon-Blood does not gain.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Thanks all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 11-22-2020, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T17:15:15-08:00","id":1425589,"title":"","content":"Forcing the maximum eight rerolls requires the attacker to roll at least five 1s and three 2s which is awfully rare, especially against a Lunar who can likely reroll at least three 1s. It\u2019s the element-changing I\u2019d quash, that\u2019s not something you get to do just because you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T17:55:00-08:00","id":1425594,"title":"","content":"any advise on how to create evocations based on an artifact?<br /> <br /> obviously the the book of wonders gives idea\\s based on magical materials but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-22T19:38:25-08:00","id":1425612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1425594#post1425594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">any advise on how to create evocations based on an artifact?</div> </div> </div> </div>My process is more or less as follows:<br /> <br /> 1) Decide the dot level of the artifact. This will inform the breadth and themes of the evocations. Remember the guidelines from Arms of the Chosen: 3 dots gives you an artifact that enhances your skill and allows supernatural effects, but usually dependent on your skill; 4 dots generally creates a whole playstyle or mechanic that a character can be built around; 5 dots is story-shaking power that bends the narrative to center around them, at least part of the time; and NA-rated ones can break normal setting rules and deliver vast power.<ul><li>Let's say you want to make a 4-dot artifact, something a character could be pretty much built around.</li> </ul><br /> 2) Work out either a general theme for the artifact, or a backstory that informs what it does. Then, do whichever one you didn't just do, using the first to work it out.<ul><li>For example, we could decide that the artifact theme we want is a powerbow whose arrows transform into falcons, which can attack independently, or serve as scouts, carry messages, etc. From that, we can imagine an artifact made from green jade or moonsilver (both of which have affinity for animals), and borne by a Dragon-Blooded scout from a Threshold kingdom, who used it to hunt a terrible Fair Folk behemoth that was terrorizing her land. We'll call it Accipiter.</li> </ul><br /> (Optional step) 3) This isn't as relevant for 3-dot artifacts, but for 4- and higher-dot ones, it's useful to consider how the evocations will generally shape playstyle as essence increases. You don't need to work out any specific evocations, but deciding now what general sort of effects are available at each Essence level will help you structure the evocation trees. Also, in this step, determine if you want there to only be one tree (possibly with branches), or multiple trees that involve exploring different aspects of the object's power.<ul><li>For Accipiter, we'll go with just a single tree. We decide we'll go for basic archery enhancing attacks and combat-useful birds at the earlier levels, and then segue into more long-lasting and general utility bird-summoning effects at slightly higher Essence levels. Since the bow was originally used by a hero to fight the Fair Folk, and to play into the whole &quot;hawks have excellent eyesight&quot; thing, we'll give the bow extra bonuses against Fair Folk, especially penetrating their glamours and illusions, at all levels.</li> </ul>4) Now that you've got your framework, it's time to start working out individual evocations. An important note at this stage is that you absolutely <i>don't</i> have to work them all out ahead of time, and in fact it's probably best if you don't. Every evocation is supposed to be a unique thing for the character wielding that artifact, a way they've figured out to use its power. It should be informed, not only by the themes and backstory of the artifact, but how the <i>current</i> holder is actually using it. So it's often good to wait a bit and figure out how the character is actually using the artifact, and build charms that support that, while still staying inside the themes and description you've worked out.<br /> <br /> That said, you should definitely build the artifact's attunement bonus (the unique benefit the character gets just from attuning to it), and probably the first evocation or two (especially if the attunement bonus is just &quot;unlock the first evocation for free&quot;. In general, try to stay one or two evocations &quot;ahead&quot; of the player, presenting them with their next options to buy after they've learned one.<ul><li>For Accipiter's attunement bonus, we decide that the user can see through the arrows it's fired, at least a little bit. For every attack made with the bow during a combat, the user gets +1 non-charm bonus die to spot concealed characters or otherwise overcome stealth. This is limited to the higher of (3 or Essence), except against Wyld creatures, in which case the bonus is uncapped.</li> <li>The first evocation will involve improving archery simply: a supplemental charm that increases the bonus to attacks with the powerbow from taking the Aim action by +1. The second charm will allow the user to spend some motes and willpower to make a decisive attack with the bow that transforms the arrow into a falcon that can then attack independently (unless it's killed).</li> </ul>When you're building the evocations, balance them against other charms, just like any other custom charm design. One thing to keep in mind, though, is resonance. In general, the effects of a resonant evocation should be roughly comparable to a Solar-level charm, a neutral evocation should be about Celestial tier (Lunars are your point of comparison here), and a dissonant one is Terrestrial power level (that is, Dragon-Blooded, at least right now). Don't make every evocation resonant, and I tend to keep them for later in the tree, too. However, the higher the dot level of an artifact, the more evocations can be resonant and the earlier they'll happen. If you're designing an artifact for a PC, only worry about the relevant level of resonance, however. If it's for a Solar, or another Exalt type using the magical material they're resonant with, you basically only have to worry about determining which evocations will have resonant-level effects, not dividing the actual effect up into separate base and resonant effects. If they're neutral, just design everything at the neutral level. And if they're dissonant, just pick which evocations are dissonant, and design at that power level from the start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T02:12:05-08:00","id":1425682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1425589#post1425589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forcing the maximum eight rerolls requires the attacker to roll at least five 1s and three 2s which is awfully rare, especially against a Lunar who can likely reroll at least three 1s. It\u2019s the element-changing I\u2019d quash, that\u2019s not something you get to do just because you want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13313_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13313\" data-vbnamecard=\"13313\">Sith_Happens</a>, appreciated!<br /> <br /> To be honest I\u2019m kinda okay with the aspect change considering what they\u2019d be having to pay to do it. This is the first time a request like this has come up with us and the players are already at E3 so I wouldn\u2019t exactly describe it as shenanigans, and it\u2019s not like there\u2019s not precedent for altering/adding to a charm\u2019s aspect: Light-as-Clouds Method does it for Hopping Firecracker Evasion at Dodge 3, Essence 2; Flesh-Sealing Flame Technique does it for Wound-Closing Technique at Medicine 3, Essence 2; Salamander Swallow Flames does it for Dragonfly Finds Mate at E3, Elusive Dragon-God Dispersion does it for Unassailable Body of Fire and Hopping Firecracker Evasion (albeit at E5); and those are ones I remember without reaching for a pdf.<br /> <br /> I am minded to make it so you can only apply the re-rolls based on 1s <i>or</i> 2s but you get to choose which after you\u2019ve seen the attack roll and make it E3 \u2013 although the last point is kind of moot for our game. The Wandering Deathknight, for example, with his massive Excellency but no re-rolls, would have trouble against this as it stands.<br /> <br /> Cheers again though, I do completely get where you\u2019re coming from and if aspect switching requests were even an \u2018every now and then\u2019 thing then I\u2019d completely agree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1425612#post1425612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loads of cool stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>This was great. Just wanted to have that registered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24647,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","user":"Moss Reynholm","date":". 11-23-2020, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T08:08:41-08:00","id":1425735,"title":"","content":"<b>PRAYER FOR NEW LIFE</b><br /> <br /> A difficult 3 ritual used by the more knowledgeable and well trained mid wives, often those who are hired by nobles and rich merchants.<br /> This short and efficacious prayer grants a 1 success bonus on any roll to survive childbirth. Including fighting off infections and bleeding. Often especially used by female politicians and nobles who wish to remain on their feet even after a difficult childbirth (the rite speeds up recovery).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-23T20:01:23-08:00","id":1425839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1425682#post1425682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and it\u2019s not like there\u2019s not precedent for altering/adding to a charm\u2019s aspect:</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Charms all have clear reasons to add those particular elements based on what they do, most obviously the ones where you\u2019re cauterizing wounds with your hands or catching fire in your firewand. Not at all the same thing as \u201cCan this Blade-Deflecting Palm repurchase that makes it do more of what it already does be Earth just because I\u2019m tired of it messing up my Rolling Boulder Blows?\u201d<br /> <br /> Heck, if you\u2019re still looking for a nerf for \u201cMore rerolls\u201d one of the obvious ways to go is \u201cBy expending your water aura.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-24T01:44:51-08:00","id":1425877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1425839#post1425839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those Charms all have clear reasons to add those particular elements based on what they do</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'd be much happier if this had elemental variants that did elemental things rather than being generic.<br /> <br /> It's fine to have a multi-element block, but IDK, maybe<br /> Water Aura rerolls 1&amp;2s, Fire Aura burns away Initiative, etc..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T01:21:53-08:00","id":1426803,"title":"","content":"<b>LANGUAGE TEA</b> (Look man, I don't have a creative streak here. Help me out). <br /> <br /> In the depths of Malfeas, there are still issues with language. Sometimes there's a dialect issue. Sometimes the words are just plain incomprehensible; the words of a crystalline demon of SWLIHN who communicates in tings and bell chimes is near impossible for a street-smart blood ape to decipher, or the words of a metagoan demon who communicates using spores tinged with specific chemicals which serve as words. Or a demon that can communicate only in the written words speaking to a demon that is blind. <br /> <br /> Either way, the variation in Malfeas means that talking to one another can be a pain. And so there comes the language tea. It isn't difficult to make, a mere difficulty 3 roll with the requirement of an exotic ingredient involving language, such as the wings of a Oktato or the bristles of a Varrotu. Difficult and expensive in Creation, but in the world-realm of Malfeas where Essence users abound and exotic ingredients literally can be picked up from the ground or rain from the sky, this is actually rather cheap.<br /> <br /> The tea is boiled, and left to cool, and then drunk/ swallowed/ splashed on/ poured onto or whatever way to make a contact with a demon. This lets the demon in question 'speak' the language for a moment, even when it is impossible. Maybe they don't have a mouth or even a solid body, but the sounds will come out, and it will be comprehensible to the other person drinking Language Tea with them.<br /> <br /> This enables people of incredibly different dialect and backgrounds to converse. Not just in language, but in intention. It would not serve as mightily as some of the charms of the Exalted, but if a Bloodape says that your blood looks boiling and hot, you would know that it is not a threat but instead a compliment. <br /> <br /> In Creation proper, this is an expensive tea costing roughly Resources 4 to purchase. And that's the issue in that it requires the expenditure of a exotic ingredient, for a benefit that is temporary. Something useful for negotiations with recalcitrant mighty elementals or in diplomatic settings with empires, but not something to be used for a conversation with the foreign neighbour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:18:22-08:00","id":1430756,"title":"","content":"NIGHTWALKER PASTE (Resources 4/ Weird thaumaturgy shit)<br /> <br /> A specialised black paste traditionally created by tribesmen deep in the linowan forests. In areas where the forest covers the sky, light is if not much use. Placed in a single black band over the eyes, this grants a +2 char dice bonus when in shadows or in a dark area, but in bright direct light, this turns into a -2 penalty. This is a Resources 3, in a linowan forest or the east, and Resources 4 elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 01-02-2021, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:24:35-08:00","id":1430758,"title":"","content":"Not bad. Is the bonus to non-Join Battle Awareness rolls? Or does it benefit any roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:42:15-08:00","id":1430761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1430758#post1430758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not bad. Is the bonus to non-Join Battle Awareness rolls? Or does it benefit any roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh crap. that's certainly something I've never considered. <br /> <br /> What do you think? I want them to be for Linowan shadow assassins, or any other kind of assassin that's like, sneaky and fast. I'm leaning towards 'any roll'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-02T10:52:51-08:00","id":1430764,"title":"","content":"&quot;Any roll&quot; is a bit much, especially if it's at no mote cost. Also I'd probably have it count as Charm dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-05T13:08:01-08:00","id":1431207,"title":"","content":"I could use some help fine tuning this custom Dragon-Blooded Charm. Based on Radiant Basilisc Jewel from Fangs at the Gate p289. I upped the pre-reqs, limited by elemental aspect and not being able to socket other gems into your body (and thus dropping Dependent stones out of the running). Then it seemed too weak, so I made it work like a Hearthstone Amulet for Jade Artifacts. I think it fits in concept, but would love feedback:<br /> <br /> Dragon Gem Formation<br /> <b>Cost:</b> -; <b>Mins:</b> Occult 5, Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Fivefold Resonance Sense x2<br /> <br /> Through study of the flow of elemental energy throughout Creation, the Dragon-Blooded becomes more aware of the power within their own veins and learns to shape the meridians of her body much like raising a manse upon a demesne. Upon purchasing this Charm, she manifests a standard or greater hearthstone matching her elemental Aspect which reflects her inner nature (her Defining Intimacies, Favored Abilities, bloodline, etc.). The hearthstone appears somewhere on her body, merged with her flesh, and providing its benefits as if socketed into an artifact. Hearthstones that enhance weapons apply their benefit to her unarmed attacks while hearthstones that enhance armor apply to her natural soak. If attuned to a jade artifact she may treat the hearthstone as being socketed into that artifact instead -- applying the benefits to that artifact as well as counting for Dependent hearthstones that might be socketed into that artifact, or for providing power for artifacts which require a hearthstone.<br /> <br /> She may not manifest Dependent hearthstones but may manifest any other kind (including Linked hearthstones, counting as the manse which sustains them) of the appropriate element. She always enjoys the increased mote recovery for being in an attuned greater demesne (Exalted, p. 160). Such hearthstones are indestructible while the Terrestrial lives and cannot be removed from her body, but shatter upon her death unless they are Steady. The Storyteller should veto hearthstone choices that are overpowered if made permanent in this fashion.<br /> <br /> [edit]<br /> <br /> Whilst we're here...<br /> <br /> I really want Deebs to have a Super Saiyan Charm like Solar Brawl's Ascendant Battle Visage. So I stripped out the movement benes (double move on rush, instant movement on Clash, rush with Strength on double-7s), weakened the &quot;cannot be Crashed&quot; to be in line with the protection Legendary Size gets, and upped the cost. I transferred the cost reduction on &quot;punch real good&quot; and energy attacks to the Deeb anima powers, signature brawl charms, and elemental bolt attack. Then I subbed in all the benefits of Embracing the Violent Flow, which are significant but way less than what you get with ABV (and the reflexive, discounted activation of OFB+AFB). Then, because possibly the main benefit of EVF is that it works with Martial Arts, I thought I'd better throw the Form tag on this. Then I *<i>possibly</i>* overtooled it by adding in an extra elemental bonus. I know this is a god-awful wall of text charm, but Deeb charms are so willpower and action hungry, I couldn't write a good charm that worked with their powerset without writing an essay. Any thoughts?<br /> <br /> Version 1<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Totemic Battle Embrace<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 25m, 3a, 1WP; <b>Mins:</b> Brawl 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Become the Hammer, Embracing the Violent Flow and one other Signature Brawl Charm<br /> <br /> The eye of the hurricane and heart of the fire, the Dragon-Blooded steps into their iconic anima, merging it with their physical form. Their appearance changes as the raw elemental power of their soul is bared to the world: a fire aspect\u2019s hair might erupt into flames and her skin might take on the hues of fire. During this time, her anima remains fixed at the burning level, neither falling to glowing or dim, nor rising to bonfire (and thus not causing anima flux). She waives any anima cost of her native Brawl Charms and Charms which match her Aura state (if any). She also enjoys the free benefit of her anima power as if she were at bonfire.<br /> <br /> For the duration of the Charm, the Dragon-Blooded may only be Crashed by attacks delivered from Close range or which have 10 or more dice of post-soak damage (other attacks leave her on 1i, though the attacker still gains initiative normally). She may Clash any attack against her, but this counts as her combat action. Clashing an attack made by an opponent who is out of range does not result in damage to that opponent, but they take the penalty from losing the Clash as normal.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood takes no penalties for flurrying unarmed attacks with other physical actions such as rushing toward an enemy or using a feat of strength to smash her way through to her target.<br /> <br /> When attacking unarmed, she may make attacks at up to Short range (lashing bolts of essence blasting from her barely contained anima), Essence tendrils grant her natural attacks the Disarming and Flexible tags (Exalted, p. 586), she adds a non-Charm success on both attack and damage rolls, and adds (Strength) Overwhelming to her Withering attacks.<br /> <br /> If she knows the Charm Elemental Bolt Attack, she may use Brawl instead of Archery or Thrown to attack with bolts of essence (including when using Charms with Elemental Bolt Attack as their prerequisite) \u2013 these attacks enjoy a 1m discount, but do not count as \u201cunarmed\u201d attacks.<br /> <br /> This Charm is compatible with Martial Arts styles that use unarmed attacks. Its elemental aspect matches the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s own. Users gain an additional elemental benefit based the on aspect of the Signature Charm used as this Charm\u2019s prerequisite:<br /> <br /> Air (Flying Whirlwind Razor): The user gains double-8s on Rushes and Disengages. If they already have double-8s, they add a non-Charm success instead.<br /> Earth (Crater-Making Impact): The user\u2019s Smash attacks do not cost Initiative or penalize defense.<br /> Fire (Erupting Fury Barrage): The user may roll an extra die of damage for every 10 that appears on their damage roll, to a maximum of (Essence) extra dice.<br /> Wood (Body of Deadly Thorns): Her Decisive attacks expose her enemies to her anima flux toxin (Damage 2i/round, Duration (Essence + Stamina) rounds, and a \u22121 penalty).<br /> <br /> This Charm subsumes and duplicates the benefits of Embracing the Violent Flow: it does not stack with Embracing the Violent Flow.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Okay, Version 1 was definitely overtooled. Version 2 takes it back to Embracing the Violent Flow, and builds from there.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Totemic Battle Embrace<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 20m, 3a, 1WP; <b>Mins:</b> Brawl 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Become the Hammer, Embracing the Violent Flow and one other Signature Brawl Charm<br /> <br /> The eye of the hurricane and heart of the fire, the Dragon-Blooded steps into their iconic anima, merging it with their physical form. Their appearance changes as the raw elemental power of their soul is bared to the world: a fire aspect\u2019s hair might erupt into flames and her skin might take on the hues of fire. Both the Dragon-Blooded and her iconic anima remain identifiable in this fused form. During this time, her anima remains fixed at the bonfire level and will not fall to burning or lower: however, she only sheds light as if at burning level and does not cause anima flux, internalizing the elemental power instead. She waives any anima cost of her native Brawl Charms and Charms which match her Aura state (if any).<br /> <br /> This Charm subsumes and duplicates the benefits of Embracing the Violent Flow: it does not stack.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blooded\u2019s natural attacks the Disarming and Flexible tags (Exalted, p. 586), she adds a non-Charm success on both attack and damage rolls, and adds (Strength) Overwhelming to her Withering attacks.<br /> <br /> The Dragon-Blood takes no penalties for flurrying unarmed attacks with other physical actions such as rushing toward an enemy or using a feat of strength to smash her way through to her target.<br /> <br /> She may also make attacks at up to Short range (lashing bolts of essence blasting from her barely contained anima). Such attacks are rolled as normal unarmed attacks, but they count as Essence attacks for effects like Salamander Swallows Flames (WFHW p166) or Fire-Eating Fist (Core p279).<br /> <br /> Additionally, her unarmed attacks use the traits of artifact weapons and channel an additional effect based on the aspect of the Signature Brawl Charm used as the prerequisite:<br /> <br /> Air (Flying Whirlwind Razor): May make unarmed attacks out to Medium range, though doing so requires an Aim action as normal.<br /> Earth (Crater-Making Impact): Grants unarmed attacks the Smashing tag. If they already have the Smashing tag, then waive the cost and defense penalty of Smash attacks.<br /> Fire (Erupting Fury Barrage): The user may roll an extra die of damage for every 10 that appears on their damage roll, to a maximum of (Essence) extra dice.<br /> Wood (Body of Deadly Thorns): A character that takes decisive damage from it is exposed to wood anima poison with Damage 2i/round, Duration (Essence + Stamina) rounds, and a \u22121 penalty.<br /> <br /> This Charm is compatible with Martial Arts styles that use unarmed attacks. Its elemental aspect matches the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s own.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's very word-y. Slightly nerfed. Version 3:<br /> <br /> Version 3<br /> <br /> Totemic Battle Embrace<br /> <b>Cost:</b> - (+5m, +3a); <b>Mins:</b> Brawl 5, Essence 5<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Aura<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisites: </b>Become the Hammer, Embracing the Violent Flow and one other Signature Brawl Charm<br /> <br /> This Charm upgrades Embracing the Violent Flow, allowing the Dragon-Blooded spend an additional +5m +3a when activating it. This removes the need for a large body of water, increases the duration to scene-long, and changes the Charm\u2019s elemental aspect to match the Dragon-Blooded\u2019s own (this cosmetically changes the manifestation of the Charm\u2019s element).<br /> <br /> The eye of the hurricane and heart of the fire, the Dragon-Blooded steps into their iconic anima, merging it with their physical form. Their appearance changes as the raw elemental power of their soul is bared to the world: a fire aspect\u2019s hair might erupt into flames and her skin might take on the hues of fire. Both the Dragon-Blooded and her iconic anima remain identifiable in this fused form. During this time, her anima remains fixed at the bonfire level and will not fall to burning or lower: however, she only sheds light as if at burning level and does not cause anima flux, internalizing the elemental power instead. She waives the anima cost of Currents Sweep to Sea, Body of Deadly Thorns, and Smashing Tidal Wave Technique, as well as for Elemental Bolt Attack and Charms derrived from it \u2013 the elemental manifestation infused with her body sufficing for such techniques.<br /> <br /> Upon taking this form, she explodes with elemental power. All characters within Close range must test against a one-time elemental hazard dealing 5L at Difficulty 5 to resist, and those who fail their roll are knocked back one range-band. The Dragon-Blooded\u2019s Sworn Kin are immune.<br /> <br /> She may not use Form-type Charms whilst under the effect of Totemic Battle Embrace, but her whilst in Aura state her Brawl-based unarmed attacks use the traits of artifact weapons.<br /> <br /> Finally, her unarmed attacks channel an additional effect based on the aspect of the Signature Brawl Charm used as the prerequisite:<br /> <br /> Air (Flying Whirlwind Razor): May make unarmed attacks out to Medium range, though doing so requires an Aim action as normal.<br /> Earth (Crater-Making Impact): Grants unarmed attacks the Smashing tag. If they already have the Smashing tag, then waive the cost and defense penalty of Smash attacks.<br /> Fire (Erupting Fury Barrage): The user may roll an extra die of damage for every 10 that appears on their damage roll, to a maximum of (Essence) extra dice.<br /> Wood (Body of Deadly Thorns): A character that takes decisive damage from it is exposed to wood anima poison with Damage 2i/round, Duration (Essence + Stamina) rounds, and a \u22121 penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 01-07-2021, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T14:15:09-08:00","id":1431500,"title":"","content":"Lack of Systems mastery is the devil.<br /> <br /> <b>Confusion-inflicting Strategem</b><br /> Cost: 4m, 1wp<br /> Mins: War 3, Essence 2<br /> Type: Reflexive<br /> Keyword: None<br /> Duration: Instant<br /> Prerequisite charms:<br /> <br /> The solar gazes upon the armies of her enemies, her preternatural skill in warfare allowing her to seek out weaknesses and fault lines in an enemy army and their strategems. Upon inflicting magnitude loss upon her enemies, she rolls her war + intelligence with double 8s, versus her the enemy's war + intelligence (the enemy can use her own charms to attempt to counter this). Upon success, it turns out her own attack has destroyed or nullified the enemy's own abilities. Supply lines are destroyed, chains of command are broken, officers killed, units scattered or isolated, and the fog of war leads to panic and friendly fire. The enemy army gains a -3 penalty for [Essence] turns to all actions as they slowly reform and reorganise themselves. With a willpower surcharge, this penalty also applies to static values.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 01-10-2021, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T15:32:13-08:00","id":1431510,"title":"","content":"Penalty to all actions right?<br /> <br /> If the penalty also applies to static values, I think this is fine. If it isn't meant to penalize static values, I'd drop the Willpower cost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T15:46:32-08:00","id":1431513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431510#post1431510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Penalty to all actions right?<br /> <br /> If the penalty also applies to static values, I think this is fine. If it isn't meant to penalize static values, I'd drop the Willpower cost.</div> </div> </div> </div>... by static values, you mean things like 'defense' and such, right? Not things like Magnitude, Training, or Might?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T16:22:46-08:00","id":1431517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431513#post1431513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... by static values, you mean things like 'defense' and such, right? Not things like Magnitude, Training, or Might?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Defense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-08T17:02:42-08:00","id":1431520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431517#post1431517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>How about a willpower surcharge for extra power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-10T11:31:35-08:00","id":1431717,"title":"","content":"GHOST SMOKE<br /> <br /> A small lantern filled with an incense composed of Hashish, spices, and Shadowland herbs, the ghost smoke comes from the thick smoke that billows from a candle when the incense is burnt. The bluish-grey smoke rapidly billows and fills the room, rapidly covering everywhere with the spicy scent. This lasts for 24 hours, and extends up to long range. The smoke is near transparent to mortal eyes, and creates a glowing silhouette of any dematerialized entity that is caught within it, reducing the penalty to hitting a dematerialized entity to -1, similar to attacking someone in a light fog. This is only a silhouette, and does not show any identifying features like the face, eye colour, or uniform. Thus all attempts to identify the entity that is caught in ghost smoke suffers a -3 penalty, leading to more than a few times when an exorcist has accidentally assaulted a god or wandering elemental.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T01:04:32-08:00","id":1431804,"title":"","content":"Um, being dematerialized isn't like being invisible - it's the physical state of not presently being in a body that's made up of matter. Even if the smoke can reveal the outline of your immaterial form, most exorcists will still be unable to strike you, penalty or no penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T05:25:33-08:00","id":1431818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431804#post1431804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um, being dematerialized isn't like being invisible - it's the physical state of not presently being in a body that's made up of matter. Even if the smoke can reveal the outline of your immaterial form, most exorcists will still be unable to strike you, penalty or no penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was discussing this Thaumaturgical Ritual with Accelerator on Discord.<br /> <br /> This effect does not let you strike immaterial spirits. But it's intended for use with the Exorcist QC in the Corebook who has their own ability to strike immaterial targets.<br /> <br /> I think this is fine, and intend to use it in my games. This is just the sort of thing that would make a mortal NPC useful to the Exalted without overshadowing them.<br /> <br /> (Minor nitpick -- most elementals can't go immaterial anymore.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T08:29:39-08:00","id":1431836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431818#post1431818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> (Minor nitpick -- most elementals can't go immaterial anymore.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yippeee! Someone's using my stuff!<br /> <br /> Also, wtf? Why can't they go immaterial? Why did they remove it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T10:35:51-08:00","id":1431849,"title":"","content":"<b>DRUG-HARDENING REGIME (3, Medicine, 3, 1 week)</b><br /> <br /> A resources 3/4 expenditure. Designer alchemical solutions are pumped into a subject, and the patient is put into a series of stances, exercises, and punches to toughen him up and induce growth. Muscle turns thick and bulky, and bones harden and thicken. The patient can now has double the soak. During this time the doctor patiently measures the subject's meridians, dispenses the right dosages of drugs, and carefully alters his diet to include metals and ceramics and protein","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 01-12-2021, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T11:11:48-08:00","id":1431852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431836#post1431836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, wtf? Why can't they go immaterial? Why did they remove it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they're physical creatures.<br /> <br /> Elementals have always been physical creatures. They can still enter spirit sanctums in 3E. But there's not any reason for them to be immaterial.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T12:19:34-08:00","id":1431856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431849#post1431849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The patient can now soak lethal with his full stamina, while he can adds 2 dice to his stamina for resisting bashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You already soak lethal damage with your full Stamina in 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T12:25:21-08:00","id":1431859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431856#post1431856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You already soak lethal damage with your full Stamina in 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. So they changed it. <br /> <br /> Well, this alchemical regiment is more fitting for 2e anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-11T21:50:58-08:00","id":1431917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431859#post1431859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. So they changed it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Turns out that having your soak change based on what kind of damage is coming in is unnecessary bookkeeping, and that\u2019s before you factor in attack-enhancing Charms that cut some of it out, or defensive Charms that raise it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T08:26:31-08:00","id":1431971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1336895-homebrew-charms-spells-evocation-gallery?p=1431917#post1431917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turns out that having your soak change based on what kind of damage is coming in is unnecessary bookkeeping, and that\u2019s before you factor in attack-enhancing Charms that cut some of it out, or defensive Charms that raise it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well then I'll just change it up. Think a +3 soak to lethal is good?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-12T11:27:50-08:00","id":1431987,"title":"","content":"[placeholder name] Artifact 3<br /> <br /> Story: In a village far from the center, a Dragonblooded exalted as an earth aspect. At first a humble smith, he created a wonders for his nearby family and friends, making shelter, clothing, food, and other useful tools. The village flourished, and he prided himself on creation, instead of destruction like so many prided themselves. And then it all changed when the Fae attacked. People were carried off, screaming into the darkness, and he himself was only kept alive by the sacrifice of his blood-family. <br /> <br /> Weeping, he threw himself into battle. But he always remembered the words of his grandfather, who told him that destruction must beget creation. And so he made the [placeholder] in memory of a smith, who must burn wood to forge steel. To destroy in order to make something greater. Baptised in the dreams of a fair folk, the blood of a demigod, and of sacred orichalcum, the hammer served him well in his first century of life. He went on to create newer, better things. But as a last favor, he crafted the hammer to accept mortals. He did not want it to languish in a armory like so many artifacts, and he did not want to leave it in the care of a Dragonblooded that might not be worthy of it; besides, he never believed in the hogwash about dragonblooded being more inherently spiritually advanced than mortals anyway. <br /> <br /> Attunement benefit: Is an artifact warhammer that is faster and deadlier than its appearance would suggest. <br /> <br /> Evocations: <br /> <br /> Lets the hammer be used as an exceptional tool to carry out any act of craft. Smashing it onto a chunk of meat would cook it. Stirring a pot with it would carry out alchemical procedures. You can use it to turn a chunk of stone into a sculpture. No time alteration though. <br /> <br /> Hammer can be used to create alterations to terrain, at the cost of essence/ initiative. Walls can be knocked down. Pit traps can be created instantaneously. Terrain can be turned into stable concrete or sleek stone in a moment. Cover can be made instantaneously. <br /> <br /> Hammer now adds a +2 to any relation to crafting (making a fort, crafting an artifact, or designing a vase) and grants an extra means for sorcerous working. <br /> <br /> Hammer now turns its enemies into useful bits, with a value of +1 to their essence. Murdering an entire coteries of bandits can leave you with things like freshly hammered swords and other things worth Resources 2. Murdering high powered ghosts and elementals would leave you with jewellery, gemstones, and killing a fae that has Essence 5 will leave you with an artifact. (this needs to be revamped to avoid abuse)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}